{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PACUuFaPBc5tDQhZcZ43Vz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018C6W4sPbfvuXushmHdqY73","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260527T022433/median/imagined_experiments.yaml","content":"tier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Median 档核心特征：exit collapse + routing gradient 被接受为 solid findings，但 CF sensitivity 因 metric incomparability\n  成为主要软肋。具体而言，TracVLA/NORA 的 trained（Cohen's d on action MSE）vs untrained（cosine dist on hidden states）\n  使用完全不同的度量空间，1-2 位 reviewer 将此视为 serious limitation，要求只报告 OpenVLA 的 within-metric comparison\n  作为 \"fair\" evidence（Δ=0.04-0.24，适中但非 dramatic）。Exit collapse 在 VLM→VLA 转换中 6/6 一致\n  （TracVLA+NORA），在 VLA→VLA 转换中 0/4（OpenVLA），形成干净的二元分离——但 1 位 reviewer 认为 Δ>0.10 阈值需要\n  principled justification（为什么不是 0.05 或 0.15？）。至少 1 位 reviewer 明确要求 behavioral/closed-loop\n  validation。\"So what for practitioners\" 被认为回答不足——routing insight 尚未转化为 actionable design guidance。\n  Rebuttal 策略围绕三点展开：(1) threshold sensitivity analysis（0.05/0.10/0.15 三阈值下 pattern 稳定性），\n  (2) 对 behavioral gap 的诚实回应（representational analysis 是 necessary first step），(3) NLP control\n  的 specificity argument 强化。C3 (vision encoder geometry) 降为 appendix observation，headline 聚焦\n  exit collapse 的 VLM→VLA transition specificity。预期 reviewer 均分 5.5-6.5，accept probability 0.25-0.50，\n  需要 1 位 champion reviewer 推动。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: plan_001_siglip_projector_rsa\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO——证明 action-relevant geometric structure 源自 frozen vision encoder，\n      LLM processing 实际降低 RSA。C1 framework 的基础数据点。Median 档下此结果不受争议，作为方法论框架的一部分被接受。\n    expected_results:\n      siglip_projector_rsa: 0.6153\n      bootstrap_95_ci: [0.5257, 0.6954]\n      trained_with_inst_peak_rsa: 0.4876\n      untrained_with_inst_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      ordering: \"SigLIP+proj (0.615) >> VLA trained (0.488) ≈ VLA untrained (0.485) >> DINO (0.388)\"\n      llm_degradation_magnitude: 0.127\n      reviewer_reception: \"A1 holds — 跨架构覆盖被接受。此实验为 C1 framework 提供 anchor point。\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 C1 framework 不是争议焦点——causal mask 对 token specialization 的数学必然性已在 D060 中承认，\n      论文贡献重新定位为\"系统实验框架\"而非\"发现\"。SigLIP RSA=0.615 >> VLA ~0.49 的 gap（Δ≈0.13）确认 frozen\n      vision encoder 是 action-relevant structure 的来源，LLM 不是 passthrough 而是实际降解 geometric alignment。\n      这个结论在 3 种分析方法（RSA、R²、CKA）下都成立——DINO 始终最低。Reviewers 接受此框架因为：(a) factorial design\n      清晰，(b) 4 种互补分析方法提供 convergent evidence，(c) 结论本身不 overreach（承认是 verification 而非 discovery）。\n      不会有 reviewer 挑战这个结果。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Vision Encoder RSA Hierarchy\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"RSA\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SigLIP+Projector\", \"0.615\", \"[0.526, 0.695]\"]\n          - [\"VLA Trained (peak L12)\", \"0.488\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"VLA Untrained (peak L12)\", \"0.485\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"DINO cls_token\", \"0.388\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 4 条件的 RSA 值，SigLIP 显著高于 VLA 两条件，VLA 高于 DINO。Error bars 标注 bootstrap CI。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C1 framework 在 median 档是最安全的贡献。Reviewers 认可 framework 的可复用性（适用于任何 decoder-only VLA）\n      和 verification 价值（排除了 residual stream leakage）。但 framework 贡献本身不足以 carry the paper——\n      它需要 C2 的 empirical findings 作为 payoff。对 acceptance 无负面影响。\n\n  - name: plan_002_dino_baseline\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      DINOv2 standalone baseline RSA——提供 non-VLA vision model 参照。DINO 在 C3 cross-encoder ranking 中\n      排名最高（RSA=0.692 cls_token），但在 backbone 内 feature 层面排名不同。\n    expected_results:\n      temporal_distance_rho_pooled: 0.833\n      per_task_rho_mean: 0.9008\n      action_probe_R2: 0.687\n      rsa_cls_token: 0.692\n      rsa_patch_mean: 0.631\n      subtask_macro_auc: 0.9717\n      cross_traj_rho: 0.65\n      control_permutation_rho: 0.039\n      reviewer_reception: \"Baseline accepted without question. DINO > CLIP ranking under RSA supports C3 observation.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      DINO baseline 在 median 档无争议。RSA=0.692（cls_token）在 cross-encoder comparison 中排最高，但这是\n      \"under RSA\" qualified 的——CKA 下 DINO 排最低。Median 档下 1-2 位 reviewer 正是利用这种 metric divergence\n      来质疑 C3 的 robustness，但 DINO baseline 本身的数据没有问题。Action probe R²=0.687 和 subtask AUC=0.972\n      说明 DINO 作为 standalone vision model 已有很强的 action-relevant structure——这反而是 C1 narrative 的\n      supporting evidence（\"vision encoder 是 action structure 的来源\"）。控制实验（permutation ρ=0.039 ≈ 0）\n      确认 probe 不是 fitting noise。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"DINOv2 Baseline Metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Note\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA (cls_token)\", \"0.692\", \"Highest in cross-encoder ranking under RSA\"]\n          - [\"RSA (patch_mean)\", \"0.631\", \"\"]\n          - [\"Action probe R²\", \"0.687\", \"Comparable to SigLIP+Projector\"]\n          - [\"Per-task ρ mean\", \"0.901\", \"Strong temporal structure\"]\n          - [\"Permutation control ρ\", \"0.039\", \"Null baseline ≈ 0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DINO per-layer feature 只有 1 层（final），无 per-layer curve。在 cross-encoder bar chart 中作为 reference bar。\"\n    analysis: >\n      DINO baseline 的双面角色：(1) 在 RSA 下排最高，支持 C3 \"highest geometric foundation\" claim（但需 \"under RSA\" qualifier），\n      (2) 在 CKA 下排最低，被 reviewer 用来质疑 C3 metric robustness。Median 档下 C3 已降为 qualified observation，\n      DINO 数据本身不是问题——metric interpretation 才是。\n\n  - name: plan_003_perlayer_rsa_curve\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      Per-layer RSA curve (L0-L32)——追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹。\n      核心发现：trained image_mean 呈 inverted-U（L0=0.612→L12=0.628 peak→L32=0.422），\n      untrained 单调衰减。Median 档下此结果被 reviewer 接受但仅在 \"under RSA\" qualification 下——CKA 不复制此 pattern。\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean:\n        peak_layer: 12\n        peak_rsa: 0.628\n        L0_rsa: 0.612\n        L32_rsa: 0.422\n        pattern: \"inverted-U\"\n        rise_delta: 0.016\n        decline_delta: 0.206\n      untrained_image_mean:\n        peak_layer: 0\n        peak_rsa: 0.612\n        L32_rsa: 0.545\n        pattern: \"monotonic_decay\"\n      trained_last_preaction:\n        peak_layer: 12\n        peak_rsa: 0.643\n      projector_rsa: 0.615\n      proj_to_L1_drop: \"0.13-0.25 (20-40%)\"\n      cka_divergence: \"CKA shows monotonic increase, NOT inverted-U — metric-dependent\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"C3 accepted as observation with 'under RSA' qualifier. Rise phase Δ=0.016 too small to be convincing.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-layer RSA curve 是 C3 的核心 evidence，但在 median 档下被降为 qualified observation。原因：\n      (1) Rise phase 极小（Δρ=0.016，CI 可能包含 0），reviewer 质疑其 practical significance；\n      (2) Decline phase 虽大（Δρ=-0.206），但 CKA 单调递增无 decline，说明 \"decline\" 是 RSA-specific；\n      (3) Training 将 peak 从 L0 移到 L12，但 trained vs untrained 的 best-vs-best Δ=+0.017 不显著\n      （CI includes 0）。这些数值让 reviewers 接受 inverted-U 作为 \"RSA 下的 observation\"，但拒绝将其作为\n      \"architecture-invariant finding\"。Median 档 reviewer 平均分 5.5-6.5 对应的态度是：\n      \"interesting observation, properly qualified, not a core contribution.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Per-layer RSA Profile Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Peak Layer\", \"Peak RSA\", \"Exit RSA (L32)\", \"Δ(rise)\", \"Δ(decline)\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained image_mean\", \"L12\", \"0.628\", \"0.422\", \"+0.016\", \"-0.206\", \"Inverted-U\"]\n          - [\"Untrained image_mean\", \"L0\", \"0.612\", \"0.545\", \"—\", \"-0.067\", \"Monotonic decay\"]\n          - [\"Trained last_preaction\", \"L12\", \"0.643\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Inverted-U\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP+Projector\", \"—\", \"0.615\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Single layer\"]\n      - title: \"RSA vs CKA Divergence\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Trained Pattern\", \"DINOv2 Ranking\", \"Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA\", \"Inverted-U (L12 peak)\", \"Highest (0.692)\", \"Geometric alignment peaks mid-layer\"]\n          - [\"CKA\", \"Monotonic increase\", \"Lowest (0.066)\", \"Global structure preserved/enhanced through layers\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Per-layer RSA curve: trained (red) 呈经典 inverted-U，peak 在 L12；untrained (blue) 从 L0 单调衰减。\n        Projector RSA (0.615) 作为 dashed horizontal reference line。标注 rise phase Δ=0.016 和 decline Δ=-0.206。\n        第二条 y-axis 或 inset panel 显示 CKA 单调递增以对比。\n    analysis: >\n      Median 档下 per-layer RSA 的价值在于支持 R² inverted-U（plan_011）的 convergent validity——\n      两个独立 metric（RSA + R²）在 trained condition 下都显示 mid-layer peak。但 RSA 特有的 rise phase 太小，\n      CKA 反转使得 \"non-monotonic refinement\" 不能作为 metric-independent claim。论文将 RSA inverted-U 放在\n      Results 正文但 qualified with \"under RSA\"，CKA divergence 在 same section 内 acknowledge（不只 appendix）。\n\n  - name: plan_004_output_head_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      Output head 权重分析——确认 SigLIP+projector frozen，LLM 权重变化均匀分布在全部 32 层。\n      排除 shallow adaptation hypothesis（action head 是否 dominate weight changes）。\n    expected_results:\n      vision_backbone:\n        rel_change: 0\n        cos_sim: 1.0\n        verdict: \"IDENTICAL\"\n      projector:\n        rel_change: 0\n        cos_sim: 1.001\n        verdict: \"IDENTICAL\"\n      llm_layers:\n        mean_rel_change: 1.3156\n        std: 0.3759\n        range: [1.22, 1.37]\n        cos_sim: 0.2178\n      head_lm_head:\n        rel_change: 1.4754\n        head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n      shallow_adaptation_gate: \"FAIL (ratio 1.12x, threshold 3x)\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"Accepted. Confirms frozen encoder, supports C1 framework.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Output head analysis 在 median 档无争议。Vision backbone + projector cos_sim=1.0 确认这些组件\n      在 trained vs untrained 之间完全 identical——这解释了为什么 RSA 在 projector output 层面 trained ≈ untrained\n      （plan_001）。LLM 权重变化均匀分布（rel_change 1.22-1.37 across all 32 layers），head 不是 special\n      （ratio 1.12x << 3x threshold），排除了 \"VLA 只在 action head 做浅层 adaptation\" 的假说。\n      注意 caveat：这里的 comparison 是 pretrained Llama-2 + fine-tune vs random init，不是 fine-tuned vs\n      pre-fine-tuning。Differences 被 pretrained vs random 的巨大差异 dominate。Reviewer 不会挑战这个结果，\n      但也不会给额外 credit——它是 expected sanity check。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Weight Change Analysis by Component\"\n        columns: [\"Component\", \"Count\", \"Mean rel_change\", \"cos_sim\", \"Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Vision backbone\", \"685\", \"0\", \"1.0\", \"IDENTICAL\"]\n          - [\"Projector\", \"6\", \"0\", \"1.001\", \"IDENTICAL\"]\n          - [\"LLM (32 layers)\", \"288\", \"1.316\", \"0.218\", \"Uniform change\"]\n          - [\"Action head (lm_head)\", \"1\", \"1.475\", \"0.000\", \"Not special (1.12x ratio)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-component rel_change bar chart 显示 vision+projector 为 0，LLM 各层 ~1.3 均匀分布，head 略高但不显著。\"\n    analysis: >\n      支持 C1 framework 的 sanity check。在 median 档下不是争议焦点，也不是 contribution。\n      其主要价值是为\"训练改变的是 LLM 的 routing 而非 encoder 的 representation\"提供 weight-level evidence。\n\n  - name: plan_005_six_probing_methods\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证。Status: orphaned——被后续更精细的实验（plan_011 full-layer R²、\n      cross-architecture validation 等）superseded。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"orphaned\"\n      original_conclusion: \"All 6 methods consistent: trained ≈ untrained >> DINO\"\n      superseded_by: [\"plan_011 (full-layer R²)\", \"cross-architecture R² probing (D088-D094)\"]\n      reviewer_reception: \"不出现在最终论文中。方法论被吸收到 C1 framework 和 C2 evidence 中。\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Plan_005 在项目早期定义，旨在系统验证 trained ≈ untrained 的 RSA invariance。随着项目演化，\n      该假说从 \"trained ≈ untrained in RSA\" 转为 \"trained ≠ untrained in routing and R² exit collapse\"，\n      原始 6-method 验证不再对应当前 narrative。核心实验被拆分为更精确的 per-layer R² scan（plan_011）\n      和跨架构 validation（D088-D094）。Median 档下 orphaned 状态不影响论文——所有有用的数据已被后续实验覆盖。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Orphaned experiment。不影响 median 档评估。\"\n\n  - name: plan_006_instruction_ablation\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      去除 instruction text 测 RSA 变化——验证 image token 位置的 RSA 是否依赖 instruction presence。\n      结论：Δ=0.004 << 0.10 threshold，instruction 无影响。\n    expected_results:\n      no_inst_untrained_peak_rsa: 0.4802\n      with_inst_untrained_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n      with_inst_trained_peak_rsa: 0.4876\n      delta_with_minus_no_inst: 0.0044\n      gate_judgment: \"FAIL — Δ=0.0044 << 0.10\"\n      interpretation: \"Image token RSA is vision-driven, not instruction-driven\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"Supports C1 token specialization. Not controversial.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Instruction ablation 确认 image token 位置的 action-relevant structure 完全来自 vision encoder，\n      与 instruction presence 无关（Δ=0.004 << 0.10）。这在 median 档下被 reviewers 接受为 C1 framework\n      的验证——causal mask 保证 image tokens 无法 attend to instructions，这个实验 empirically 验证了\n      即使 residual stream 理论上可能 leak information，实际上不存在 leakage。\n      结合 plan_007（2×2 matrix）和 plan_008（random instruction），形成三重不变性：\n      training × instruction presence × instruction content 都不影响 image token RSA。\n      Reviewer 将此视为 thorough methodology（positive signal），但不是 novel finding。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Instruction Ablation — RSA Invariance\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Peak RSA\", \"Δ from with-inst\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained + instruction\", \"0.488\", \"reference\"]\n          - [\"Untrained + instruction\", \"0.485\", \"-0.003\"]\n          - [\"Untrained - instruction\", \"0.480\", \"-0.004\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer RSA curves: with-instruction vs without-instruction 几乎完全重叠。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C1 framework 的 supporting evidence。Median 档下 reviewer 认可实验设计的 thoroughness，\n      但 Δ=0.004 是 expected result（causal mask guarantees it），不构成 surprise 或额外 contribution。\n\n  - name: plan_007_2x2_training_instruction_matrix\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      2×2 factorial design (training × instruction)——四条件全收敛在 RSA 0.48-0.49 band。\n      Bootstrap CI includes 0，确认 neither training nor instruction 对 image token RSA 有显著影响。\n    expected_results:\n      full_2x2_matrix:\n        trained_with_inst: 0.4876\n        trained_no_inst: 0.489\n        untrained_with_inst: 0.4846\n        untrained_no_inst: 0.4802\n      training_effect_with_inst: 0.003\n      training_effect_no_inst: 0.0088\n      instruction_effect_trained: -0.0014\n      instruction_effect_untrained: 0.0044\n      bootstrap_delta_ci: \"[-0.058, 0.072] includes 0\"\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      reviewer_reception: \"Clean factorial design accepted. Supports 'architecture matters, training/instruction don't (for RSA)' narrative.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      2×2 matrix 是 C1 framework 的 capstone evidence——四条件收敛在 0.48-0.49 band（range=0.009），\n      远小于 VLA-vs-DINO gap（~0.10）。Bootstrap CI [-0.058, 0.072] 包含 0 确认无统计显著差异。\n      在 median 档下这个结果被 reviewer 接受但也被理解为：\"RSA 对 training 不敏感\"恰恰意味着 RSA\n      不是测量 training effect 的正确 metric——R²（plan_011）才是。这种理解实际上 SUPPORTS 论文的\n      narrative arc：RSA measures geometric alignment（encoder-dominated），R² measures functional\n      information（training-sensitive）。两者的 dissociation 本身是 finding。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Factorial RSA Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"With Instruction\", \"No Instruction\", \"Instruction Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained\", \"0.488\", \"0.489\", \"-0.001\"]\n          - [\"Untrained\", \"0.485\", \"0.480\", \"+0.004\"]\n          - [\"Training Effect\", \"+0.003\", \"+0.009\", \"\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 interaction plot: 两条近似平行的水平线（training 和 no-training），instruction presence 在 x-axis，RSA 在 y-axis。四个点聚集在 0.48-0.49 band。\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSA 的 training-instruction 不变性在 median 档下是 double-edged：\n      (+) 确认 C1 framework 的 clean result，(−) 也意味着 RSA 不能区分 trained/untrained effect，\n      C3 的 \"training improves RSA\" claim 不成立。Reviewer 接受结果但将 C3 降级。\n\n  - name: plan_008_random_instruction_control\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Random/shuffled/empty instruction 替代真实 instruction——验证 instruction content 不影响 RSA。\n      完成三重不变性：training + instruction presence + instruction content。\n    expected_results:\n      normal_peak_rsa: 0.4888\n      empty_peak_rsa: 0.4723\n      random_peak_rsa: 0.4835\n      shuffled_peak_rsa: 0.4832\n      max_absolute_delta: 0.0165\n      instruction_invariant: true\n      all_peak_at_L16: true\n      reviewer_reception: \"排除 trivial separability 攻击面。Thoroughness appreciated.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random instruction control 排除了\"probe 利用 instruction content 的 trivial 差异做分类\"的攻击面。\n      All 4 conditions 在 ±0.017 内，peak 都在 L16，确认 image token RSA 对 instruction content 完全不变。\n      Empty 略低（-0.017）可解释为 sequence length 变化导致的 positional embedding shift，不是 semantic effect。\n      Median 档下 reviewer 认可这个 control 的 thoroughness——它回应了 potential concern \"10-way classification\n      might trivially succeed by detecting instruction content in residual stream\"。但 reviewer 也指出：\n      RSA 不变性只说明 image tokens 不 encode instruction info，不说明 instruction tokens 如何 route——\n      后者是 C2 的 domain（probe accuracy + attention profiling）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Instruction Content Invariance\"\n        columns: [\"Instruction Type\", \"Peak RSA\", \"Peak Layer\", \"Δ from Normal\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Normal\", \"0.489\", \"L16\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Random words\", \"0.484\", \"L16\", \"-0.005\"]\n          - [\"Shuffled tokens\", \"0.483\", \"L16\", \"-0.006\"]\n          - [\"Empty string\", \"0.472\", \"L16\", \"-0.017\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4 条件 per-layer RSA curves 密集重叠，仅 empty 略低。标注 max Δ=0.017。\"\n    analysis: >\n      完成 C1 三重不变性。Median 档 reviewers 给 credit for methodological rigor，但此实验不直接贡献\n      到 median 档的核心 tension（CF metric incomparability, behavioral gap, threshold justification）。\n\n  - name: plan_009_cka_verification\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      CKA 指标重复 RSA 发现——检验 metric independence。结论：PARTIAL——CKA ordering 反转 RSA ordering\n      (untrained > trained > projector > DINO)。RSA-CKA dissociation 本身成为 finding。\n    expected_results:\n      linear_cka:\n        untrained_img_mean_L23: 0.0894\n        trained_img_mean_L23: 0.0834\n        projector: 0.0809\n        dino: 0.0664\n        trained_last_preaction_L32: 0.127\n      rdm_cka:\n        trained_img_mean_L23: 0.2599\n        projector: 0.2568\n        untrained_img_mean_L23: 0.2464\n        dino: 0.2408\n        trained_last_preaction_L32: 0.2898\n      key_findings:\n        - \"DINO lowest across all metrics (robust)\"\n        - \"CKA: untrained > trained (reversed from RSA)\"\n        - \"last_preaction >> image_mean in CKA (redistribution confirmed)\"\n      rsa_cka_dissociation: >\n        RSA captures geometric alignment (LLM degrades it from projector).\n        CKA captures global structure preservation (LLM maintains/enhances it).\n        Two metrics measure different aspects — dissociation is informative, not contradictory.\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        Critical for median 档 C3 qualification. 1-2 reviewers use CKA reversal to\n        argue C3 inverted-U is metric-dependent, forcing 'under RSA' qualifier.\n    result_rationale: >\n      CKA verification 是 median 档 C3 降级的关键 evidence。RSA 说 LLM 降解 geometric alignment\n      （projector 0.615 >> VLA 0.488），CKA 说 LLM 保持 global structure（untrained > trained ≈ projector > DINO）。\n      这不是矛盾——RSA 和 CKA 测量不同属性：RSA 基于 rank correlation 捕捉 pairwise distance structure，\n      CKA 捕捉 linear alignment of similarity matrices。但 reviewers 有理由质疑：如果 C3 claim 是\n      \"inverted-U refinement\"，而 CKA 显示单调递增，那 \"refinement\" 这个词只在 RSA 下成立。\n      Median 档 reviewer R2/R3 正是利用这一点将 C3 从 \"finding\" 降为 \"observation\"。\n      但 DINO consistently lowest across RSA 和 CKA 说明 \"VLA >> DINO\" 是 metric-robust 的。\n      last_preaction CKA >> image_mean CKA 确认 information redistribution to instruction tokens（C2 evidence）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSA vs CKA Ordering Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Rank\", \"RSA Ordering\", \"Linear CKA Ordering\", \"RDM-CKA Ordering\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1st\", \"Projector (0.615)\", \"Untrained (0.089)\", \"Trained last_pre (0.290)\"]\n          - [\"2nd\", \"Trained (0.488)\", \"Trained (0.083)\", \"Trained img (0.260)\"]\n          - [\"3rd\", \"Untrained (0.485)\", \"Projector (0.081)\", \"Projector (0.257)\"]\n          - [\"4th\", \"DINO (0.388)\", \"DINO (0.066)\", \"DINO (0.241)\"]\n      - title: \"RSA-CKA Dissociation Interpretation\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"What It Measures\", \"LLM Effect\", \"Training Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA\", \"Pairwise geometric alignment\", \"Degrades\", \"Negligible\"]\n          - [\"CKA\", \"Global structure preservation\", \"Preserves\", \"Slight reduction\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-panel: left = RSA ordering bar chart, right = CKA ordering bar chart, with connecting lines showing rank reversal for projector vs untrained.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA verification 是 median 档 narrative 的 pivotal experiment——它迫使 C3 从 core claim 降为 observation。\n      但 RSA-CKA dissociation 本身可以被 frame 为 positive finding：\"LLM degrades geometric alignment while\n      preserving global structure, suggesting different representational transformations at different levels of analysis.\"\n      Reviewer R1 (champion) 可能认可这种 nuanced interpretation；R4 (skeptic) 会说 \"pick one metric and commit.\"\n\n  - name: plan_010_libero_spatial_benchmark\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展——在第二个 benchmark 上验证 RSA inverted-U 和 R² profile。\n      确认 cross-benchmark robustness。\n    expected_results:\n      rsa:\n        trained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 14, rsa: 0.691}\n        trained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 15, rsa: 0.695}\n        untrained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 0, rsa: 0.652}\n        untrained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 1, rsa: 0.666}\n        pattern: \"Trained inverted-U confirmed; untrained flat/declining\"\n      action_probe:\n        trained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 13, R2: 0.696}\n        trained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 21, R2: 0.675}\n        untrained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 0, R2: 0.673}\n        untrained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 1, R2: 0.635}\n        untrained_collapse: \"L5-L31 R² ≈ -0.015, only L32 recovers to 0.621\"\n      bootstrap:\n        best_vs_best_imgmean: {delta: 0.023, ci: [0.012, 0.036], p: 0.001}\n        best_vs_best_lastpre: {delta: 0.040, ci: [0.019, 0.057], p: 0.0004}\n      cross_benchmark_consistency:\n        rsa_peak_goal: \"L12\"\n        rsa_peak_spatial: \"L14-15\"\n        probe_peak_goal: \"L8-13\"\n        probe_peak_spatial: \"L13-21\"\n        verdict: \"High consistency — peak layers within 2-layer range\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"Cross-benchmark replication strengthens C2. Reviewers give credit for consistency.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      LIBERO-Spatial replication 在 median 档下为 C2 exit collapse 和 routing findings 提供 cross-benchmark\n      support。RSA inverted-U peak 从 Goal 的 L12 移到 Spatial 的 L14-15（within 3-layer window），\n      R² peak 从 L8-13 移到 L13-21（wider but overlapping）。Bootstrap significance 全部 p < 0.001。\n      Untrained 的 last_preaction collapse（L5-L31 R² ≈ -0.015）比 Goal benchmark 更 dramatic——\n      随机 LLM 权重在中间层完全破坏了 action-decodable structure。\n      Median 档 reviewers 认可 cross-benchmark consistency（\"not a benchmark-specific artifact\"），\n      但注意这只是 OpenVLA 单架构的两个 benchmarks——跨架构验证（D088-D094）才是真正解决 RC4 的关键。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark Peak Layer Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"LIBERO-Goal\", \"LIBERO-Spatial\", \"Δ layers\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA peak (trained)\", \"L12\", \"L14-15\", \"2-3\"]\n          - [\"R² peak image_mean (trained)\", \"L8\", \"L13\", \"5\"]\n          - [\"R² peak last_pre (trained)\", \"L13\", \"L21\", \"8\"]\n          - [\"R² peak image_mean (untrained)\", \"L0\", \"L0\", \"0\"]\n      - title: \"LIBERO-Spatial Significance Tests\"\n        columns: [\"Comparison\", \"Δ\", \"95% CI\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Best-vs-best image_mean\", \"+0.023\", \"[0.012, 0.036]\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"Best-vs-best last_preaction\", \"+0.040\", \"[0.019, 0.057]\", \"0.0004\"]\n          - [\"Same-layer L13 image_mean\", \"+0.711\", \"[0.685, 0.740]\", \"0.001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Dual-panel overlay: Goal (solid) vs Spatial (dashed) per-layer R² curves for trained condition.\n        Both show inverted-U with peaks in L8-L21 range. Untrained collapse visible in both benchmarks.\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark 验证增强 C2 robustness。Median 档 reviewer 给 credit 但指出这仍是 single-architecture\n      (OpenVLA) 验证。真正的 cross-architecture evidence 来自 D088-D094 的 TracVLA + NORA 实验。\n\n  - name: plan_011_fulllayer_r2_scan\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: >\n      33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 full-layer R² scan。\n      核心发现：R² inverted-U（trained peaks L8-L13），exit collapse（trained R² 在 exit 层下降），\n      untrained L10-L13 pathological collapse。这是 C2 exit collapse finding 的 foundational experiment。\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean:\n        peak_layer: 8\n        peak_R2: 0.6553\n      trained_last_preaction:\n        peak_layer: 13\n        peak_R2: 0.6779\n      untrained_image_mean:\n        peak_layer: 0\n        peak_R2: 0.6403\n      untrained_last_preaction:\n        peak_layer: 32\n        peak_R2: 0.6093\n      bootstrap_best_vs_best:\n        image_mean: {delta: 0.015, p: 0.006}\n        last_preaction: {delta: 0.069, p: 0.0001}\n      rsa_vs_r2_alignment:\n        trained_imgmean: \"RSA peak L12, R² peak L8 — 4-layer offset\"\n        trained_lastpre: \"RSA peak L12, R² peak L13 — near-aligned\"\n        untrained_lastpre: \"RSA peak L1, R² peak L32 — maximally divergent\"\n      exit_collapse_openvla:\n        trained_delta_peak_exit_imgmean: ~0.07\n        trained_delta_peak_exit_lastpre: ~0.07\n        note: >\n          OpenVLA 是 VLA→VLA transition (OXE→LIBERO)。v3 MCCV 修正后 Δ=0.033-0.086，\n          均 < 0.10 threshold。Exit collapse 在 VLA→VLA 转换中不显著。\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        Median 档的核心支撑。R² inverted-U 作为 metric-independent finding 被接受（与 RSA convergent）。\n        但 A2 partially: 1 位 reviewer 要求 Δ>0.10 threshold 的 principled justification。\n    result_rationale: >\n      Full-layer R² scan 是论文最重要的实验之一。在 median 档下：\n      (1) R² inverted-U（trained peaks L8-L13）与 RSA inverted-U（L12）convergent——两个独立 metric\n      都显示 mid-layer peak，这是 metric-independent 的 evidence；\n      (2) Trained vs untrained 的 best-vs-best Δ=+0.069（last_preaction, p<0.0001）在 R² 上是显著的\n      （而 RSA Δ=+0.017 不显著），确认 R² 比 RSA 更 sensitive to training effects；\n      (3) Untrained L10-L13 pathological collapse（R² ≈ 0 或负值）是 random LLM weights 的 artifact——\n      结构化的 pretrained weights 不产生这种 collapse；\n      (4) 但对 OpenVLA 而言（VLA→VLA transition），exit collapse 的 Δ 在 v3 MCCV 修正后仅 0.033-0.086，\n      低于 Δ>0.10 threshold。这成为 A2 partial 的基础——reviewer 质疑 threshold 选择的 principled justification。\n      Cross-architecture validation（TracVLA Δ=0.138-0.294, NORA Δ=0.302-0.691）中 VLM→VLA 转换\n      的 exit collapse 远更 dramatic，使得 exit collapse 作为 VLM→VLA transition 的 signature 被 65-85% reviewer 接受。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Full-layer R² Peak Comparison (OpenVLA, LIBERO-Goal)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Readout\", \"Peak Layer\", \"Peak R²\", \"Exit R² (L31/32)\", \"Δ(peak−exit)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained\", \"image_mean\", \"L8\", \"0.655\", \"~0.58\", \"~0.07\"]\n          - [\"Trained\", \"last_preaction\", \"L13\", \"0.678\", \"~0.61\", \"~0.07\"]\n          - [\"Untrained\", \"image_mean\", \"L0\", \"0.640\", \"~0.58\", \"~0.06\"]\n          - [\"Untrained\", \"last_preaction\", \"L32\", \"0.609\", \"0.609\", \"0\"]\n      - title: \"R² vs RSA Convergence\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"R² Peak Layer\", \"RSA Peak Layer\", \"Offset\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained image_mean\", \"L8\", \"L12\", \"4 layers\"]\n          - [\"Trained last_preaction\", \"L13\", \"L12\", \"1 layer\"]\n          - [\"Untrained image_mean\", \"L0\", \"L0\", \"0 (aligned)\"]\n      - title: \"Threshold Sensitivity (median 档 rebuttal 所需)\"\n        columns: [\"Threshold\", \"VLM→VLA Cells Passing\", \"VLA→VLA Cells Passing\", \"Separation Clean?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Δ > 0.05\", \"6/6\", \"2/4\", \"Partial — 2 OpenVLA cells leak through\"]\n          - [\"Δ > 0.10\", \"6/6\", \"0/4\", \"Clean binary separation\"]\n          - [\"Δ > 0.15\", \"5/6\", \"0/4\", \"1 TracVLA Spatial (0.138) drops out\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Per-layer R² profile (4 curves: trained/untrained × image_mean/last_preaction).\n        Trained curves 显示 inverted-U with mid-layer peak；untrained image_mean 从 L0 单调衰减；\n        untrained last_preaction 有 L10-L13 pathological collapse zone。\n      - >\n        Threshold sensitivity plot: x-axis = threshold value (0.05, 0.10, 0.15),\n        y-axis = cells passing. 两条线（VLM→VLA 和 VLA→VLA）在 0.10 处实现完美分离。\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_011 是 C2 exit collapse 的 foundational experiment。Median 档下的关键 tension：\n      OpenVLA 自身的 exit collapse Δ（0.033-0.086）低于 0.10 threshold，这并非因为 exit collapse\n      不存在于 OpenVLA，而是因为 OpenVLA 的 untrained 条件是 OXE-pretrained VLA（而非 pure VLM）——\n      exit collapse 已经在 OXE training 时发生过一次。这恰恰支持 \"exit collapse is a one-time VLM→VLA\n      reorganization\" 的 narrative。1 位 reviewer 要求 threshold sensitivity analysis 来证明\n      Δ>0.10 不是 cherry-picked——rebuttal 应展示 0.05/0.10/0.15 三个 threshold 下 pattern 的稳定性，\n      其中 0.10 实现最干净的 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 二元分离。\n\n  - name: plan_012_clip_vit_control\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 作为 vision encoder——区分 VL pretraining 贡献 vs encoder quality。\n      结论：CLIP < DINO in both RSA and R²。VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised（DINOv2）。\n    expected_results:\n      unified_hyperparams: \"epochs=50, patience=5, lr=1e-3, batch=256, hidden=256, seed=42\"\n      clip_cls_mean_R2: 0.5866\n      dino_cls_mean_R2: 0.6343\n      projector_mean_R2: 0.6298\n      vla_image_mean_L19_R2: 0.5986\n      vla_last_preaction_L19_R2: 0.6711\n      ordering: \"vla_last_preaction_L19 > dino_cls ≈ projector > vla_image_mean_L19 > clip_cls\"\n      clip_vs_dino_p: 0.0\n      clip_rsa: 0.557\n      dino_rsa_cls: 0.692\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        Accepted. CLIP < DINO invalidates 'VL pretraining provides superior action structure' hypothesis.\n        This is an honest negative result that adds credibility to the paper.\n    result_rationale: >\n      CLIP ViT-L control 在 median 档下产生重要的 negative result：VL pretraining（contrastive image-text\n      alignment）不比 self-supervised pretraining（DINOv2）提供更好的 action-relevant structure。\n      CLIP RSA=0.557 < DINO patch_mean 0.631 < DINO cls 0.692。R² 同样 CLIP (0.587) < DINO (0.634)。\n      这个 negative finding 在 median 档下被 reviewers 积极评价——它表明论文不 cherry-pick positive results，\n      愿意 report 对 initial hypothesis 不利的 evidence。DINOv2 的优势可能来自其 self-distillation\n      训练目标对 spatial-geometric 特征的保留优于 CLIP 的 global image-text alignment。\n      这个结果直接影响 C3 论述：DINOv2 ranking 只在 RSA 下成立（CKA 反转），且不能归因于 VL pretraining。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Encoder Action Probe R² (Unified Hyperparameters)\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder/Source\", \"Mean R²\", \"vs Projector p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"VLA last_preaction L19\", \"0.671\", \"0.002\"]\n          - [\"DINOv2 cls_token\", \"0.634\", \"0.557 (n.s.)\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP+Projector\", \"0.630\", \"reference\"]\n          - [\"VLA image_mean L19\", \"0.599\", \"0.000\"]\n          - [\"CLIP ViT-L cls_token\", \"0.587\", \"0.000\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 5 sources ordered by R², with pairwise significance brackets. CLIP clearly lowest among non-VLA sources.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CLIP control 在 median 档下增强论文 credibility。Honest negative result = reviewer trust。\n      但也限制了 C3 叙事——不能 claim \"VL pretraining is key\"，只能 claim \"DINOv2 provides\n      highest geometric foundation under RSA, regardless of VL pretraining.\"\n\n  - name: plan_013_branch_split_rsa\n    plan_id: plan_013\n    description: >\n      Branch-split RSA——从 DinoSigLIP fused backbone 分离 DINOv2 (1088d) vs SigLIP (1088d) branch，\n      定量回答 fused backbone 中各组件的贡献。\n    expected_results:\n      dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n      siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n      fused_2176d_rsa: 0.634\n      post_projector_4096d_rsa: 0.615\n      standalone_dino_cls_rsa: 0.692\n      delta_branches: 0.002\n      fusion_benefit: \"+0.013-0.015 (complementary)\"\n      projector_compression: \"-0.019 (0.634→0.615)\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"Clean result. Both branches contribute equally. Fusion provides complementary benefit.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Branch-split 在 median 档下是 clean supporting evidence：DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP in fused backbone\n      （Δ < 0.002），说明两个分支提供 complementary 而非 redundant 的 action-relevant structure。\n      Fusion (0.634) > either branch (~0.620) 确认 complementary benefit。Projector 轻微压缩\n      (0.634→0.615) 说明 4096→4096 的 MLP 投影损失少量 geometric structure。\n      Standalone DINO cls (0.692) >> in-backbone DINOv2 (0.619) 的差异来自不同的 extraction layer\n      和 feature aggregation 方式（cls token vs backbone intermediate features），不是 backbone\n      本身的降级。这个结果在 median 档下不引起争议——它完善 C1 framework 对 vision encoder 内部结构的理解。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Branch-Split RSA Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"RSA\", \"Dimensionality\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"DINOv2 branch (in-backbone)\", \"0.619\", \"1088d\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP branch (in-backbone)\", \"0.621\", \"1088d\"]\n          - [\"Fused backbone\", \"0.634\", \"2176d\"]\n          - [\"Post-projector\", \"0.615\", \"4096d\"]\n          - [\"Standalone DINOv2 cls\", \"0.692\", \"1024d\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar showing DINOv2 + SigLIP branches composing the fused backbone, with projector compression indicated.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Branch-split 完善 C1 story。在 median 档下，reviewer 可能 briefly note \"interesting that\n      fusion helps\" 但不会 dwell on it——这是 ancillary 结果，不影响核心 C2 exit collapse + routing findings。\n\n  - name: cross_arch_r2_exit_collapse_synthesis\n    plan_id: \"D088-D102 synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      跨三架构（OpenVLA/TracVLA/NORA）× 四 suite 的 R² exit collapse 综合分析。\n      这不是 experiment_plan 中的 individual experiment，而是 D088-D102 全部完成后的 synthesis。\n      Median 档的核心 finding：VLM→VLA 转换 6/6 cells 确认 exit collapse（Δ=0.156-0.455），\n      VLA→VLA 转换 0/4 cells 超过 Δ>0.10 threshold（Δ=0.033-0.086）。\n    expected_results:\n      vlm_to_vla_cells:\n        total: 6\n        passing: 6\n        delta_range: [0.138, 0.691]\n        architectures: [\"TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\", \"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\"]\n        details:\n          tracvla_goal: {trained_delta: 0.228, untrained_delta: 0.048}\n          tracvla_spatial: {trained_delta: 0.138, untrained_delta: 0.016}\n          tracvla_object: {trained_delta: 0.294, untrained_delta: 0.009}\n          tracvla_long: {trained_delta: 0.198, untrained_delta: 0.028}\n          nora_goal: {trained_delta: 0.691, untrained_delta: 0.044}\n          nora_spatial: {trained_delta: 0.302, untrained_delta: 0.037}\n      vla_to_vla_cells:\n        total: 4\n        passing: 0\n        delta_range: [0.033, 0.086]\n        architecture: \"OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\"\n        details:\n          openvla_goal: {trained_delta: 0.086, note: \"largest but still < 0.10\"}\n          openvla_spatial: {trained_delta: 0.037, note: \"v3 MCCV corrected from 0.110\"}\n          openvla_object: {trained_delta: 0.037, note: \"v3 MCCV corrected from 0.121\"}\n          openvla_long: {trained_delta: 0.033, note: \"OFT finetuning\"}\n      nlp_control:\n        llama2_chat_delta: 0.000\n        phi3_instruct_delta: 0.000\n        qwen25_instruct_delta: 0.000\n        interpretation: \"NLP finetuning produces ZERO exit collapse — effect is VLA-specific\"\n      threshold_sensitivity:\n        threshold_005: {vlm_vla_passing: \"6/6\", vla_vla_passing: \"2/4\", clean: false}\n        threshold_010: {vlm_vla_passing: \"6/6\", vla_vla_passing: \"0/4\", clean: true}\n        threshold_015: {vlm_vla_passing: \"5/6\", vla_vla_passing: \"0/4\", clean: false}\n        optimal_threshold: \"0.10 — 唯一实现完美 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 分离的阈值\"\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        A2 partially holds: exit collapse accepted but Δ>0.10 threshold questioned by 1 reviewer.\n        Exit collapse reviewer acceptance: 0.75 (3/4 reviewers fully accept, 1 wants threshold justification).\n        NLP control significantly strengthens specificity argument.\n    result_rationale: >\n      跨架构 R² exit collapse 是 median 档论文最强的 empirical contribution。\n      VLM→VLA 6/6 vs VLA→VLA 0/4 形成干净的二元分离，解读为\"exit collapse 是 VLM→VLA 转换的 one-time\n      reorganization effect\"。NLP finetuning control（3 个 LLM backbone 均 Δ=0.000）排除了\n      \"exit collapse is a generic finetuning artifact\" 的解释。\n\n      Median 档下的 tension 集中在 threshold justification（A2 partially）：\n      - Δ>0.10 是 post-hoc 选择的——它恰好是 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 分离的 sweet spot\n      - Δ>0.05 时 OpenVLA Goal (0.086) 和 Spatial 两个 cell 会 leak through，分离不干净\n      - Δ>0.15 时 TracVLA Spatial (0.138) 会 drop out\n      - Reviewer 质疑：为什么不用 permutation-based threshold？\n\n      Rebuttal 策略：展示 0.05/0.10/0.15 三阈值下 pattern 的稳定性（核心 pattern——VLM→VLA 产生更大的\n      exit R² drop 而 VLA→VLA 不产生——在所有三个阈值下定性一致）。0.10 不是 magic number，而是\n      produce cleanest binary separation 的 empirically optimal threshold。\n\n      NLP control 是 median 档的 key defensive evidence：同 backbone 的 chat-finetuned model 完全\n      flat R² profile（≈0.155 across all layers），确认 exit collapse 是 action-oriented training specific。\n      65-85% reviewer acceptance rate 对应 3/4 reviewers accept + 1 borderline on threshold。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse Matrix: VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA Transition\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Transition Type\", \"Trained Δ\", \"Untrained Δ\", \"Collapse?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3)\", \"Goal\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.228\", \"0.048\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3)\", \"Spatial\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.138\", \"0.016\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3)\", \"Object\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.294\", \"0.009\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3)\", \"Long\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.198\", \"0.028\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL)\", \"Goal\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.691\", \"0.044\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL)\", \"Spatial\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.302\", \"0.037\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2)\", \"Goal\", \"VLA→VLA\", \"0.086\", \"0.033\", \"no\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2)\", \"Spatial\", \"VLA→VLA\", \"0.037\", \"—\", \"no\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2)\", \"Object\", \"VLA→VLA\", \"0.037\", \"0.076\", \"no\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2)\", \"Long (OFT)\", \"VLA→VLA\", \"0.033\", \"0.016\", \"no\"]\n      - title: \"NLP Finetuning Controls — Exit Collapse is VLA-Specific\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Backbone\", \"Finetuning Type\", \"R² Mean\", \"R² Range\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Llama-2-7b-chat\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"SFT+RLHF\", \"0.1553\", \"0.1547-0.1555\", \"0.000\"]\n          - [\"Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"Instruction tuning\", \"0.1555\", \"0.1552-0.1555\", \"0.000\"]\n          - [\"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\", \"Qwen2.5-3B\", \"Instruction tuning\", \"0.1554\", \"0.1550-0.1555\", \"0.000\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        3×4 heatmap: architectures × suites, color = Δ(peak−exit).\n        VLM→VLA cells (TracVLA + NORA) 全部深色（high Δ），VLA→VLA cells (OpenVLA) 全部浅色（low Δ）。\n        2 grey cells = NORA Object/Long (no checkpoint)。清晰可视化 binary separation。\n      - >\n        Threshold sensitivity plot: three thresholds (0.05, 0.10, 0.15) on x-axis,\n        VLM→VLA passing rate and VLA→VLA passing rate as two lines.\n        At 0.10, lines achieve maximum separation (6/6 vs 0/4).\n    analysis: >\n      Exit collapse synthesis 是 median 档论文的 strongest card。6/6 VLM→VLA + 0/4 VLA→VLA + 3/3 NLP = 0\n      形成三层 evidence：effect present in VLM→VLA, absent in VLA→VLA, absent in NLP finetuning。\n      这个 triple contrast 是 reviewer champion 推荐 accept 的核心理由。\n      Threshold sensitivity analysis 是 rebuttal 必备：展示 0.10 不是 arbitrary 而是 optimal separation point。\n\n  - name: cf_sensitivity_cross_architecture\n    plan_id: \"D088-D102 CF synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      跨架构 counterfactual sensitivity 综合分析——median 档的核心 weakness。\n      CF metric incomparability（A3 fails）意味着 TracVLA/NORA 的 trained (Cohen's d on action MSE)\n      vs untrained (cosine dist on hidden states) 不可比较。仅 OpenVLA 提供 fair within-metric comparison。\n    expected_results:\n      fair_comparison_openvla:\n        note: \"唯一可做 fair trained-vs-untrained 对比的架构（both conditions generate actions）\"\n        goal:\n          trained_top_d: 1.182\n          trained_top_condition: \"wrong\"\n          untrained_top_d: 1.048\n          untrained_top_condition: \"empty\"\n          delta: \"+0.134\"\n          within_condition_empty: {trained: 1.170, untrained: 1.048, delta: \"+0.122\"}\n        spatial:\n          trained_top_d: 1.173\n          trained_top_condition: \"empty\"\n          untrained_top_d: 0.936\n          untrained_top_condition: \"empty\"\n          delta: \"+0.237\"\n        object:\n          trained_d: 1.21\n          untrained: \"cosine dist — INCOMMENSURABLE\"\n          note: \"Object untrained 只有 cosine dist，不可比\"\n        long_oft:\n          trained_top_d: 0.565\n          trained_top_condition: \"shuffled\"\n          note: \"OFT: all d moderate (0.45-0.57), lower than full finetuning\"\n      trained_absolute_magnitude:\n        note: \"TracVLA/NORA trained 的 absolute Cohen's d（不与 untrained 比较）\"\n        tracvla_goal: {empty: 1.524, wrong: 1.405, shuffled: 1.336, para: 1.213}\n        tracvla_spatial: {empty: 1.327, wrong: 1.172, shuffled: 1.295, para: 1.183}\n        tracvla_object: {empty: 1.212, wrong: 1.060, shuffled: 1.164, para: 0.971}\n        tracvla_long: {empty: 1.473, wrong: 1.418, shuffled: 1.391, para: 1.161}\n        nora_goal: \"cos=1.0 (saturated)\"\n        all_d_ge_045: true\n        note2: \"所有 trained VLA 的 Cohen's d ≥ 0.45，确认 instruction sensitivity consistently present\"\n      untrained_cosine_dist:\n        note: \"TracVLA/NORA untrained 的 cosine distance（不同 metric，不与 trained d 比较）\"\n        tracvla_goal: {empty: 0.153, wrong: 0.016, shuffled: 0.084, para: 0.004}\n        tracvla_long: {empty: 0.173, wrong: 0.022, shuffled: 0.120, para: 0.007}\n        nora_goal: {empty: 0.081, wrong: 0.014, shuffled: 0.033, para: 0.004}\n        ordering: \"empty >> shuffled > wrong > para (structural > semantic for untrained VLMs)\"\n      metric_incomparability_impact:\n        incommensurable_cells: \"6/10 matrix cells\"\n        commensurable_cells: \"2/10 (OpenVLA Goal + Spatial, both use Cohen's d)\"\n        partially_commensurable: \"2/10 (OpenVLA Object, Long — untrained uses different metric or OFT confound)\"\n        reviewer_severity: \"1-2 reviewers view as serious limitation\"\n      cf_sensitivity_reviewer_acceptance: 0.45\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        A3 fails. CF sensitivity 降为 'supporting evidence with caveats'.\n        论文策略：(1) OpenVLA within-metric comparison 作为 'fair' evidence (Δ=0.04-0.24),\n        (2) TracVLA/NORA 仅报告 trained absolute magnitude (d ≥ 0.45),\n        (3) 明确承认 metric incomparability 在正文中 (不只 appendix)。\n    result_rationale: >\n      CF metric incomparability 是 median 档的核心软肋，直接导致 cf_sensitivity_reviewer_acceptance\n      仅 0.30-0.60。根本原因：TracVLA/NORA untrained 是纯 VLM，无法生成 meaningful actions，\n      所以 CF sensitivity 只能在 hidden representation space 用 cosine distance 测量。\n      而 trained VLA 可以生成 actions，CF sensitivity 用 Cohen's d on action MSE。\n      两种 metric 测量的是完全不同的东西：Cohen's d 测量 action output 的偏移量，cosine dist\n      测量 hidden state 的方向变化。\n\n      OpenVLA 是唯一 fair comparison 的架构，因为 untrained = OXE-pretrained VLA（可生成 actions）。\n      结果：Goal Δ=+0.13, Spatial Δ=+0.24。适中但非 dramatic。OXE baseline 本身已有强 CF\n      sensitivity（d≈1.0），LIBERO fine-tuning 只做边际提升。\n\n      Median 档 reviewers 的具体反应：\n      - R1 (champion): \"CF metric incomparability is acknowledged; OpenVLA fair comparison\n        shows consistent positive direction; trained absolute d ≥ 0.45 across architectures\n        confirms instruction sensitivity exists\"\n      - R2/R3 (borderline): \"Cannot claim 'training amplifies CF sensitivity' across\n        architectures when 6/10 cells use incommensurable metrics. Only OpenVLA shows\n        moderate amplification (Δ=0.04-0.24), which could be within measurement noise\"\n      - R4 (skeptic): \"CF finding is effectively single-architecture (OpenVLA) with\n        moderate effect, not a cross-architecture result\"\n\n      Rebuttal 策略：降低 CF claim 强度。从 \"training amplifies CF sensitivity\" 改为\n      \"trained VLAs consistently exhibit substantial instruction sensitivity (d ≥ 0.45)\"，\n      不做 trained-vs-untrained 跨架构 ratio comparison。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"OpenVLA Fair CF Comparison (Same Metric: Cohen's d)\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Trained Top d\", \"Untrained Top d\", \"Δ\", \"Fair?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Goal\", \"1.182 (wrong)\", \"1.048 (empty)\", \"+0.134\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"1.173 (empty)\", \"0.936 (empty)\", \"+0.237\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Object\", \"1.210 (empty)\", \"cos=0.569\", \"—\", \"NO (metric differs)\"]\n          - [\"Long (OFT)\", \"0.565 (shuffled)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"OFT confound\"]\n      - title: \"Trained VLA Absolute CF Magnitude (all architectures)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Empty d\", \"Wrong d\", \"Shuffled d\", \"Para d\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Goal\", \"1.170\", \"1.182\", \"0.763\", \"0.707\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"1.173\", \"0.885\", \"0.979\", \"0.807\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Goal\", \"1.524\", \"1.405\", \"1.336\", \"1.213\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"1.327\", \"1.172\", \"1.295\", \"1.183\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"1.212\", \"1.060\", \"1.164\", \"0.971\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"1.473\", \"1.418\", \"1.391\", \"1.161\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"saturated\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n      - title: \"Metric Incomparability Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Trained Metric\", \"Untrained Metric\", \"Comparable?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Cohen's d (action MSE)\", \"Cohen's d (action MSE)\", \"YES — both are OXE-pretrained VLAs\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Cohen's d (action MSE)\", \"Cosine distance (hidden states)\", \"NO — untrained is pure VLM\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Cohen's d (action MSE)\", \"Cosine distance (hidden states)\", \"NO — untrained is pure VLM\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Split panel: Left = OpenVLA fair comparison (paired bar chart, trained vs untrained d,\n        Goal and Spatial suites). Right = all-architecture trained absolute d (grouped bars,\n        showing d ≥ 0.45 consistently). Clear visual separation between 'fair comparison'\n        and 'absolute magnitude' evidence.\n      - >\n        Metric incomparability schematic: flowchart showing why TracVLA/NORA untrained\n        cannot produce actions → must use hidden-space cosine dist → incommensurable\n        with trained Cohen's d on action MSE.\n    analysis: >\n      CF sensitivity 在 median 档被降为 \"supporting evidence with caveats\"。论文需要在 Abstract\n      和 Results 中明确：(1) trained VLAs consistently show CF sensitivity (d ≥ 0.45),\n      (2) 但 metric incomparability 限制了跨条件 amplification 的量化,\n      (3) 仅 OpenVLA 提供 fair within-metric comparison (Δ=0.04-0.24)。\n      这种降级使 CF 从 \"core finding\" 变为 \"consistent observation\"——足以支持 routing narrative\n      但不足以独立 carry a claim。Exit collapse 因此成为唯一的 standalone core finding。\n\n  - name: three_tier_routing_gradient\n    plan_id: \"D094 synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      三层级 routing gradient 综合分析：VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA。\n      Median 档下被接受为 \"suggestive observation\" 但因只有 1 个 Tier-2 datapoint (OXE openvla-7b)\n      而被降级。\n    expected_results:\n      tier_1_vlm_base:\n        examples: [\"Phi-3-Vision (TracVLA untrained)\", \"Qwen2.5-VL (NORA untrained)\"]\n        l1_heads: \"28-32/32 (from language pretraining)\"\n        cf_sensitivity: \"cosine dist 0.01-0.17 (low, structural not semantic)\"\n        r2_exit_collapse: \"No (Δ = 0.009-0.048)\"\n        cross_instruction: \"100% at all layers\"\n        evidence_strength: \"Strong (4 VLM datapoints)\"\n      tier_2_oxe_pretrained:\n        examples: [\"openvla-7b (970K OXE episodes)\"]\n        l1_heads: \"25/32\"\n        cf_sensitivity: \"d ≈ 1.05 (strong, semantic)\"\n        r2_exit_collapse: \"No (Δ = 0.033-0.086)\"\n        cross_instruction: \"100% at all layers\"\n        evidence_strength: \"Weak (n=1)\"\n      tier_3_task_finetuned:\n        examples: [\"TracVLA trained\", \"NORA trained\", \"OpenVLA LIBERO-finetuned\"]\n        l1_heads: \"12-30 (architecture-dependent, D090)\"\n        cf_sensitivity: \"d = 0.45-1.52 (all ≥ 0.45)\"\n        r2_exit_collapse: \"VLM→VLA: YES (6/6); VLA→VLA: NO (0/4)\"\n        evidence_strength: \"Moderate to Strong (10 cells across 3 architectures)\"\n      gradient_narrative: >\n        Routing emerges at VLM→VLA transition (Tier 1→3 or 1→2) and reshapes at\n        general→task-specific transition (Tier 2→3).\n        Exit collapse marks the VLM→VLA boundary.\n        L1 heads are inherited from base model, NOT created by VLA training.\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        1 reviewer (R3) downgrades to 'suggestive observation' due to n=1 Tier-2.\n        Other reviewers accept the narrative framework but ask for additional Tier-2\n        datapoints (e.g., RT-2-X, Octo) as future work.\n    result_rationale: >\n      三层级 gradient 在 median 档下面临 n=1 Tier-2 挑战。只有 openvla-7b 代表 Tier-2\n      （OXE-pretrained but not task-specific），没有其他 general-purpose VLA pretrained checkpoint\n      可用。Reviewer R3 的质疑合理：\"one datapoint is an observation, not a gradient.\"\n\n      但 gradient 的 qualitative pattern 仍然 informative：\n      - Tier-1 (VLM): 有 language routing（L1 heads from pretraining）但无 action-relevant routing\n        （CF sensitivity 极低，无 exit collapse）\n      - Tier-2 (OXE): 有 language routing + general action routing（CF d≈1.0，但无 exit collapse）\n      - Tier-3 (task-finetuned): exit collapse 出现（VLM→VLA）或保持（VLA→VLA），CF 可能增加或不变\n\n      这三层描述了 routing 的 staged emergence：首先从 zero action-relevant routing（VLM）到\n      general routing（OXE），然后从 general 到 task-specific（LIBERO finetuning）。\n      Exit collapse 标记第一次转换的边界。\n\n      Median 档 rebuttal 策略：承认 n=1 Tier-2 的局限性，降为 \"suggestive observation warranting\n      further investigation\"，建议 future work 使用 RT-2-X 和 Octo 作为额外 Tier-2 datapoints。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Three-Tier Routing Gradient Evidence\"\n        columns: [\"Tier\", \"Example\", \"L1 Heads\", \"CF d\", \"R² Collapse?\", \"Evidence n\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1: VLM Base\", \"Phi-3 / Qwen2.5-VL\", \"28-32\", \"cos < 0.2\", \"No\", \"4 VLMs\"]\n          - [\"2: OXE Pretrained\", \"openvla-7b\", \"25/32\", \"d ≈ 1.05\", \"No\", \"1 (weak)\"]\n          - [\"3: Task-Finetuned\", \"All 3 trained VLAs\", \"12-30\", \"d ≥ 0.45\", \"6/6 VLM→VLA\", \"10 cells\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Three-panel gradient diagram: VLM → OXE → Task-finetuned on x-axis.\n        y-axis panels showing L1 heads, CF sensitivity, and exit collapse magnitude.\n        Tier-2 marked with dashed box and 'n=1' annotation.\n    analysis: >\n      三层级 gradient 在 median 档是 \"nice-to-have\" narrative framework 而非 standalone finding。\n      它为 exit collapse 提供 interpretive context（\"one-time VLM→VLA reorganization\"）但不是\n      independently validated。Accept probability 不因 gradient 增加但也不因 n=1 限制而下降——\n      reviewers 将其视为 reasonable speculation grounded in available data。\n\n  - name: l1_base_model_dependent_analysis\n    plan_id: \"D090 synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      L1 instruction-dominant heads 跨架构分析——确认 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent\n      而非 training-induced。Median 档下 A5 holds：这个区分被接受为 honest science。\n    expected_results:\n      openvla:\n        goal: {trained: \"23/32\", untrained_oxe: \"26/32\"}\n        object: {trained: \"24/32\", untrained_oxe: \"24/32\"}\n        long_oft: {trained: \"14/32\", untrained_oxe: \"25/32\", note: \"OFT reduces heads\"}\n      tracvla:\n        all_suites: {trained: \"27-30/32\", untrained_phi3: \"32/32\", note: \"Phi-3 pretraining already 32/32\"}\n      nora:\n        goal: {trained: \"13/16\", untrained_qwen: \"13/16\"}\n        spatial: {trained: \"12/16\", untrained_qwen: \"14/16\"}\n      key_distinction: >\n        Training-induced: R² exit collapse, CF sensitivity increase (for VLM→VLA).\n        Base-model-dependent: L1 head count, attention fraction.\n        This is NOT a weakness — it's honest science that strengthens credibility.\n      tracvla_mixed_heads: \"h13 and h22 consistently mixed across all 4 suites in trained models\"\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        A5 holds. Reviewers appreciate the distinction. R1 specifically credits the paper\n        for not overclaiming L1 heads as training effect.\n    result_rationale: >\n      D090 区分（training-induced vs base-model-dependent）在 median 档下被 reviewers 积极接受。\n      原因：(1) 区分本身体现 intellectual honesty——很多论文会将 L1 heads 归因于训练（因为 trained 有 24/32）\n      而忽略 untrained 也有 25/32 (OXE) 或 32/32 (Phi-3)；(2) 区分使论文的 training effect claims\n      更 precise 和 defensible——只 claim R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity（有 clean evidence），\n      不 overclaim L1 heads；(3) TracVLA 的 mixed heads (h13, h22) pattern 提供了 bonus finding——\n      training 不增加 head count 但 repurpose some heads 为 mixed-modality processing。\n\n      A5 holds 意味着 reviewers 不会用\"L1 不是训练效果\"来攻击论文——相反，他们认为这增加了论文的\n      可信度。但 reviewer A7 challenge 仍然存在：\"如果 L1 heads 来自预训练，训练到底贡献了什么\n      for practitioners？\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"L1 Instruction-Dominant Heads: Training vs Pretraining\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Trained\", \"Untrained\", \"Δ\", \"Source\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Goal\", \"23/32\", \"26/32 (OXE)\", \"-3\", \"Base-model\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Object\", \"24/32\", \"24/32 (OXE)\", \"0\", \"Base-model\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"All 4\", \"27-30/32\", \"32/32 (Phi-3)\", \"-2 to -5\", \"Base-model\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"13/16\", \"13/16 (Qwen)\", \"0\", \"Base-model\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Spatial\", \"12/16\", \"14/16 (Qwen)\", \"-2\", \"Base-model\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Paired bar chart: trained vs untrained L1 heads for each architecture.\n        Key visual: untrained bars are equal or HIGHER than trained bars in most cases,\n        demonstrating base-model origin.\n    analysis: >\n      L1 analysis 在 median 档是 credibility builder。它不增加 accept probability 但也不降低——\n      是 \"right thing to report\" 的典型例子。对 A7 challenge 的间接回应：training 的 practitioner-relevant\n      贡献不在 L1 heads（来自预训练）而在 exit collapse（marks VLA readiness）和 routing pattern\n      reshape（from mid-layer to bookend）。\n\n  - name: aggregate_median_tier_assessment\n    plan_id: \"overall synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      所有实验完成后的 aggregate assessment，对应 median 档的 reviewer scores、accept probability\n      和 rebuttal 策略。\n    expected_results:\n      claims_status:\n        C1_framework: \"Accepted (A1 holds). Framework contribution recognized.\"\n        C2_exit_collapse: >\n          Accepted with minor qualification (A2 partially).\n          6/6 VLM→VLA confirmed, 0/4 VLA→VLA confirmed. NLP control strengthens.\n          1 reviewer asks for threshold sensitivity analysis.\n        C2_routing_gradient: \"Accepted as suggestive observation (n=1 Tier-2 limits strength).\"\n        C2_cf_sensitivity: >\n          Downgraded to 'supporting evidence with caveats' (A3 fails).\n          Metric incomparability prevents cross-architecture quantification.\n          Only OpenVLA fair comparison (Δ=0.04-0.24) reported as evidence.\n        C3_vision_encoder: \"Moved to appendix as qualified observation (RSA-specific, CKA reverses).\"\n      claims_surviving_without_qualification: 2.0\n      reviewer_predictions:\n        R1_champion:\n          score: 7\n          stance: \"Accept\"\n          key_positive: \"Novel framework, exit collapse is clean finding with NLP control\"\n          key_concern: \"CF metric incomparability noted but acceptable given honest framing\"\n        R2_positive:\n          score: 6\n          stance: \"Weak Accept\"\n          key_positive: \"Cross-architecture R² collapse is convincing\"\n          key_concern: \"Threshold justification needed; practitioner implications vague\"\n        R3_borderline:\n          score: 6\n          stance: \"Borderline Accept\"\n          key_positive: \"Methodological rigor appreciated\"\n          key_concern: \"Three-tier gradient is n=1 at Tier-2; CF downgrade reduces contribution density\"\n        R4_skeptic:\n          score: 5\n          stance: \"Weak Reject\"\n          key_positive: \"Framework is useful\"\n          key_concern: \"No behavioral evidence; 'so what for practitioners?' insufficiently answered\"\n      reviewer_avg_score: 6.0\n      strong_reject_count: 0\n      accept_probability: 0.37\n      exit_collapse_reviewer_acceptance: 0.75\n      cf_sensitivity_reviewer_acceptance: 0.45\n      rebuttal_success_if_borderline: 0.50\n      rebuttal_strategy:\n        point_1: >\n          Threshold sensitivity analysis: show pattern stability across 0.05/0.10/0.15.\n          At all three thresholds, VLM→VLA consistently produces larger Δ than VLA→VLA.\n          0.10 is optimal separation point, not arbitrary cutoff.\n        point_2: >\n          Behavioral gap honest response: 'Representational analysis is a necessary first\n          step providing mechanistic hypotheses. Behavioral validation requires closed-loop\n          infrastructure (robot hardware + policy execution) that is orthogonal to our\n          analytical contribution. We commit to this as immediate future work.'\n        point_3: >\n          Strengthen NLP control specificity: 'Three NLP-finetuned controls sharing\n          identical backbones (Llama-2, Phi-3, Qwen2.5) all show flat R² ≈ 0.155 with\n          Δ = 0.000. This triple control rules out generic finetuning artifact and\n          confirms exit collapse is specific to action-oriented training.'\n        point_4: >\n          Practitioner guidance (A7): 'Our findings suggest three actionable insights:\n          (1) Exit collapse as VLA-readiness diagnostic — its presence confirms successful\n          VLM→VLA transition; (2) Entry-exit routing pattern as architecture design target —\n          VLA architectures should optimize L1 instruction capture and exit-layer action\n          conditioning; (3) Pretraining-aware fine-tuning — knowing that L1 routing is\n          inherited, practitioners can focus fine-tuning on mid-layer and exit-layer\n          representations rather than entry-layer attention.'\n      ac_assessment: >\n        AC leaning: 'The paper makes a genuine empirical contribution with the exit collapse\n        finding and cross-architecture framework. The CF metric incomparability is properly\n        acknowledged. The behavioral validation gap is a fair criticism but does not invalidate\n        the representational analysis. Recommend accept if authors address threshold\n        justification and strengthen practitioner implications in camera-ready.'\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档 reviewer avg 6.0 的组成逻辑：\n      - R1 (7): 看到了论文的 big picture value（first systematic cross-architecture VLA analysis）。\n        Exit collapse with NLP control 是 clean finding。CF caveat 被 honest framing 抵消。\n      - R2 (6): 认可 exit collapse 但对 threshold 和 practitioner implications 有 reservations。\n        Rebuttal 中 threshold sensitivity analysis 可以 address。\n      - R3 (6): 方法论 rigor 获得 respect，但 three-tier gradient 的 n=1 和 CF downgrade 使得\n        contribution density 看起来偏薄（\"one core finding + framework + observations\"）。\n      - R4 (5): 核心质疑是 behavioral gap 和 practitioner relevance。不会给 strong reject\n        但 \"representational analysis without behavioral validation\" 是 principled concern。\n\n      Accept probability 0.37 的计算：需要 R1 champion + R2 被 rebuttal 说服 + R3 接受\n      rebuttal 中的 threshold analysis + AC 决定 behavioral gap 不是 dealbreaker。\n      如果 rebuttal 成功（probability 0.50），R2→accept, R3→accept, 即使 R4 stays weak reject，\n      AC 会 follow majority。如果 rebuttal 失败，R3→reject, 变成 2-2 split，AC 可能 reject。\n\n      Claims surviving without qualification = 2.0：\n      (1) Exit collapse as VLM→VLA transition marker (fully accepted)\n      (2) Experimental framework for token-level VLA analysis (accepted as methodological contribution)\n      C2-CF 存活但 qualified，C3 移入 appendix，routing gradient 为 suggestive observation。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Median Tier Reviewer Score Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Reviewer\", \"Score\", \"Stance\", \"Primary Concern\", \"Rebuttal Target?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R1 (Champion)\", \"7\", \"Accept\", \"CF metric incomparability (minor)\", \"No — already accepts\"]\n          - [\"R2 (Positive)\", \"6\", \"Weak Accept\", \"Threshold justification + practitioner implications\", \"Yes — threshold sensitivity\"]\n          - [\"R3 (Borderline)\", \"6\", \"Borderline Accept\", \"n=1 Tier-2 + CF downgrade → thin contribution\", \"Yes — strengthen NLP control narrative\"]\n          - [\"R4 (Skeptic)\", \"5\", \"Weak Reject\", \"No behavioral evidence + practitioner gap\", \"Partially — honest future work commitment\"]\n      - title: \"Median Tier Aggregate Metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Range\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Reviewer avg score\", \"6.0\", \"[5.5, 6.5]\"]\n          - [\"Strong reject count\", \"0\", \"[0, 1]\"]\n          - [\"Accept probability\", \"0.37\", \"[0.25, 0.50]\"]\n          - [\"Claims surviving w/o qualification\", \"2.0\", \"[1.5, 2.5]\"]\n          - [\"Rebuttal success rate\", \"0.50\", \"[0.4, 0.6]\"]\n          - [\"Exit collapse reviewer acceptance\", \"0.75\", \"[0.65, 0.85]\"]\n          - [\"CF sensitivity reviewer acceptance\", \"0.45\", \"[0.3, 0.6]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Radar chart: 6 axes (novelty, rigor, significance, clarity, completeness, reproducibility).\n        Median tier scores: novelty=7 (first cross-arch VLA analysis), rigor=7 (NLP controls + factorial design),\n        significance=5 (limited by behavioral gap), clarity=7 (clean writing), completeness=5 (CF caveat + n=1),\n        reproducibility=6 (open checkpoints but complex pipeline).\n    analysis: >\n      Median 档的 bottom line：论文有一个 clean core finding（exit collapse as VLM→VLA marker）和一个\n      solid methodological contribution（cross-architecture token-level analysis framework），但 CF sensitivity\n      被 metric incomparability 削弱，behavioral validation gap 被 1 位 reviewer 视为 significant limitation。\n      Rebuttal 有 50% 机会成功——关键在于 threshold sensitivity analysis 的说服力和 AC 对 \"representational\n      analysis without behavioral validation\" 的 tolerance。CoRL 作为 robotics venue 对 behavioral evidence\n      的期望高于 pure ML venues，但 representational analysis 的 novelty 也被看重。\n      建议 rebuttal 中将 behavioral validation 定位为 \"orthogonal contribution requiring different\n      experimental infrastructure\" 而非 \"limitation of current work\"，同时用 NLP triple control\n      的 specificity 强化 VLA-specific nature of exit collapse。\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":138,"cache_read_input_tokens":98953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":138},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26867879-adf3-4c14-9393-b9045e867606","uuid":"318b5792-f190-477e-ad8c-511db8132ab2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018C6W4sPbfvuXushmHdqY73","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260527T022433/median/imagined_experiments.yaml"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26867879-adf3-4c14-9393-b9045e867606","uuid":"3c3c551b-fdb6-4785-96d2-c9431055176d","timestamp":"2026-05-27T02:46:12.448Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260527T022433/median/imagined_experiments.yaml","content":"tier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Median 档核心特征：exit collapse + routing gradient 被接受为 solid findings，但 CF sensitivity 因 metric incomparability\n  成为主要软肋。具体而言，TracVLA/NORA 的 trained（Cohen's d on action MSE）vs untrained（cosine dist on hidden states）\n  使用完全不同的度量空间，1-2 位 reviewer 将此视为 serious limitation，要求只报告 OpenVLA 的 within-metric comparison\n  作为 \"fair\" evidence（Δ=0.04-0.24，适中但非 dramatic）。Exit collapse 在 VLM→VLA 转换中 6/6 一致\n  （TracVLA+NORA），在 VLA→VLA 转换中 0/4（OpenVLA），形成干净的二元分离——但 1 位 reviewer 认为 Δ>0.10 阈值需要\n  principled justification（为什么不是 0.05 或 0.15？）。至少 1 位 reviewer 明确要求 behavioral/closed-loop\n  validation。\"So what for practitioners\" 被认为回答不足——routing insight 尚未转化为 actionable design guidance。\n  Rebuttal 策略围绕三点展开：(1) threshold sensitivity analysis（0.05/0.10/0.15 三阈值下 pattern 稳定性），\n  (2) 对 behavioral gap 的诚实回应（representational analysis 是 necessary first step），(3) NLP control\n  的 specificity argument 强化。C3 (vision encoder geometry) 降为 appendix observation，headline 聚焦\n  exit collapse 的 VLM→VLA transition specificity。预期 reviewer 均分 5.5-6.5，accept probability 0.25-0.50，\n  需要 1 位 champion reviewer 推动。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: plan_001_siglip_projector_rsa\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO——证明 action-relevant geometric structure 源自 frozen vision encoder，\n      LLM processing 实际降低 RSA。C1 framework 的基础数据点。Median 档下此结果不受争议，作为方法论框架的一部分被接受。\n    expected_results:\n      siglip_projector_rsa: 0.6153\n      bootstrap_95_ci: [0.5257, 0.6954]\n      trained_with_inst_peak_rsa: 0.4876\n      untrained_with_inst_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      ordering: \"SigLIP+proj (0.615) >> VLA trained (0.488) ≈ VLA untrained (0.485) >> DINO (0.388)\"\n      llm_degradation_magnitude: 0.127\n      reviewer_reception: \"A1 holds — 跨架构覆盖被接受。此实验为 C1 framework 提供 anchor point。\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 C1 framework 不是争议焦点——causal mask 对 token specialization 的数学必然性已在 D060 中承认，\n      论文贡献重新定位为\"系统实验框架\"而非\"发现\"。SigLIP RSA=0.615 >> VLA ~0.49 的 gap（Δ≈0.13）确认 frozen\n      vision encoder 是 action-relevant structure 的来源，LLM 不是 passthrough 而是实际降解 geometric alignment。\n      这个结论在 3 种分析方法（RSA、R²、CKA）下都成立——DINO 始终最低。Reviewers 接受此框架因为：(a) factorial design\n      清晰，(b) 4 种互补分析方法提供 convergent evidence，(c) 结论本身不 overreach（承认是 verification 而非 discovery）。\n      不会有 reviewer 挑战这个结果。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Vision Encoder RSA Hierarchy\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"RSA\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SigLIP+Projector\", \"0.615\", \"[0.526, 0.695]\"]\n          - [\"VLA Trained (peak L12)\", \"0.488\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"VLA Untrained (peak L12)\", \"0.485\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"DINO cls_token\", \"0.388\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 4 条件的 RSA 值，SigLIP 显著高于 VLA 两条件，VLA 高于 DINO。Error bars 标注 bootstrap CI。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C1 framework 在 median 档是最安全的贡献。Reviewers 认可 framework 的可复用性（适用于任何 decoder-only VLA）\n      和 verification 价值（排除了 residual stream leakage）。但 framework 贡献本身不足以 carry the paper——\n      它需要 C2 的 empirical findings 作为 payoff。对 acceptance 无负面影响。\n\n  - name: plan_002_dino_baseline\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      DINOv2 standalone baseline RSA——提供 non-VLA vision model 参照。DINO 在 C3 cross-encoder ranking 中\n      排名最高（RSA=0.692 cls_token），但在 backbone 内 feature 层面排名不同。\n    expected_results:\n      temporal_distance_rho_pooled: 0.833\n      per_task_rho_mean: 0.9008\n      action_probe_R2: 0.687\n      rsa_cls_token: 0.692\n      rsa_patch_mean: 0.631\n      subtask_macro_auc: 0.9717\n      cross_traj_rho: 0.65\n      control_permutation_rho: 0.039\n      reviewer_reception: \"Baseline accepted without question. DINO > CLIP ranking under RSA supports C3 observation.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      DINO baseline 在 median 档无争议。RSA=0.692（cls_token）在 cross-encoder comparison 中排最高，但这是\n      \"under RSA\" qualified 的——CKA 下 DINO 排最低。Median 档下 1-2 位 reviewer 正是利用这种 metric divergence\n      来质疑 C3 的 robustness，但 DINO baseline 本身的数据没有问题。Action probe R²=0.687 和 subtask AUC=0.972\n      说明 DINO 作为 standalone vision model 已有很强的 action-relevant structure——这反而是 C1 narrative 的\n      supporting evidence（\"vision encoder 是 action structure 的来源\"）。控制实验（permutation ρ=0.039 ≈ 0）\n      确认 probe 不是 fitting noise。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"DINOv2 Baseline Metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Note\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA (cls_token)\", \"0.692\", \"Highest in cross-encoder ranking under RSA\"]\n          - [\"RSA (patch_mean)\", \"0.631\", \"\"]\n          - [\"Action probe R²\", \"0.687\", \"Comparable to SigLIP+Projector\"]\n          - [\"Per-task ρ mean\", \"0.901\", \"Strong temporal structure\"]\n          - [\"Permutation control ρ\", \"0.039\", \"Null baseline ≈ 0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DINO per-layer feature 只有 1 层（final），无 per-layer curve。在 cross-encoder bar chart 中作为 reference bar。\"\n    analysis: >\n      DINO baseline 的双面角色：(1) 在 RSA 下排最高，支持 C3 \"highest geometric foundation\" claim（但需 \"under RSA\" qualifier），\n      (2) 在 CKA 下排最低，被 reviewer 用来质疑 C3 metric robustness。Median 档下 C3 已降为 qualified observation，\n      DINO 数据本身不是问题——metric interpretation 才是。\n\n  - name: plan_003_perlayer_rsa_curve\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      Per-layer RSA curve (L0-L32)——追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹。\n      核心发现：trained image_mean 呈 inverted-U（L0=0.612→L12=0.628 peak→L32=0.422），\n      untrained 单调衰减。Median 档下此结果被 reviewer 接受但仅在 \"under RSA\" qualification 下——CKA 不复制此 pattern。\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean:\n        peak_layer: 12\n        peak_rsa: 0.628\n        L0_rsa: 0.612\n        L32_rsa: 0.422\n        pattern: \"inverted-U\"\n        rise_delta: 0.016\n        decline_delta: 0.206\n      untrained_image_mean:\n        peak_layer: 0\n        peak_rsa: 0.612\n        L32_rsa: 0.545\n        pattern: \"monotonic_decay\"\n      trained_last_preaction:\n        peak_layer: 12\n        peak_rsa: 0.643\n      projector_rsa: 0.615\n      proj_to_L1_drop: \"0.13-0.25 (20-40%)\"\n      cka_divergence: \"CKA shows monotonic increase, NOT inverted-U — metric-dependent\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"C3 accepted as observation with 'under RSA' qualifier. Rise phase Δ=0.016 too small to be convincing.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-layer RSA curve 是 C3 的核心 evidence，但在 median 档下被降为 qualified observation。原因：\n      (1) Rise phase 极小（Δρ=0.016，CI 可能包含 0），reviewer 质疑其 practical significance；\n      (2) Decline phase 虽大（Δρ=-0.206），但 CKA 单调递增无 decline，说明 \"decline\" 是 RSA-specific；\n      (3) Training 将 peak 从 L0 移到 L12，但 trained vs untrained 的 best-vs-best Δ=+0.017 不显著\n      （CI includes 0）。这些数值让 reviewers 接受 inverted-U 作为 \"RSA 下的 observation\"，但拒绝将其作为\n      \"architecture-invariant finding\"。Median 档 reviewer 平均分 5.5-6.5 对应的态度是：\n      \"interesting observation, properly qualified, not a core contribution.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Per-layer RSA Profile Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Peak Layer\", \"Peak RSA\", \"Exit RSA (L32)\", \"Δ(rise)\", \"Δ(decline)\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained image_mean\", \"L12\", \"0.628\", \"0.422\", \"+0.016\", \"-0.206\", \"Inverted-U\"]\n          - [\"Untrained image_mean\", \"L0\", \"0.612\", \"0.545\", \"—\", \"-0.067\", \"Monotonic decay\"]\n          - [\"Trained last_preaction\", \"L12\", \"0.643\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Inverted-U\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP+Projector\", \"—\", \"0.615\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Single layer\"]\n      - title: \"RSA vs CKA Divergence\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Trained Pattern\", \"DINOv2 Ranking\", \"Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA\", \"Inverted-U (L12 peak)\", \"Highest (0.692)\", \"Geometric alignment peaks mid-layer\"]\n          - [\"CKA\", \"Monotonic increase\", \"Lowest (0.066)\", \"Global structure preserved/enhanced through layers\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Per-layer RSA curve: trained (red) 呈经典 inverted-U，peak 在 L12；untrained (blue) 从 L0 单调衰减。\n        Projector RSA (0.615) 作为 dashed horizontal reference line。标注 rise phase Δ=0.016 和 decline Δ=-0.206。\n        第二条 y-axis 或 inset panel 显示 CKA 单调递增以对比。\n    analysis: >\n      Median 档下 per-layer RSA 的价值在于支持 R² inverted-U（plan_011）的 convergent validity——\n      两个独立 metric（RSA + R²）在 trained condition 下都显示 mid-layer peak。但 RSA 特有的 rise phase 太小，\n      CKA 反转使得 \"non-monotonic refinement\" 不能作为 metric-independent claim。论文将 RSA inverted-U 放在\n      Results 正文但 qualified with \"under RSA\"，CKA divergence 在 same section 内 acknowledge（不只 appendix）。\n\n  - name: plan_004_output_head_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      Output head 权重分析——确认 SigLIP+projector frozen，LLM 权重变化均匀分布在全部 32 层。\n      排除 shallow adaptation hypothesis（action head 是否 dominate weight changes）。\n    expected_results:\n      vision_backbone:\n        rel_change: 0\n        cos_sim: 1.0\n        verdict: \"IDENTICAL\"\n      projector:\n        rel_change: 0\n        cos_sim: 1.001\n        verdict: \"IDENTICAL\"\n      llm_layers:\n        mean_rel_change: 1.3156\n        std: 0.3759\n        range: [1.22, 1.37]\n        cos_sim: 0.2178\n      head_lm_head:\n        rel_change: 1.4754\n        head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n      shallow_adaptation_gate: \"FAIL (ratio 1.12x, threshold 3x)\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"Accepted. Confirms frozen encoder, supports C1 framework.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Output head analysis 在 median 档无争议。Vision backbone + projector cos_sim=1.0 确认这些组件\n      在 trained vs untrained 之间完全 identical——这解释了为什么 RSA 在 projector output 层面 trained ≈ untrained\n      （plan_001）。LLM 权重变化均匀分布（rel_change 1.22-1.37 across all 32 layers），head 不是 special\n      （ratio 1.12x << 3x threshold），排除了 \"VLA 只在 action head 做浅层 adaptation\" 的假说。\n      注意 caveat：这里的 comparison 是 pretrained Llama-2 + fine-tune vs random init，不是 fine-tuned vs\n      pre-fine-tuning。Differences 被 pretrained vs random 的巨大差异 dominate。Reviewer 不会挑战这个结果，\n      但也不会给额外 credit——它是 expected sanity check。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Weight Change Analysis by Component\"\n        columns: [\"Component\", \"Count\", \"Mean rel_change\", \"cos_sim\", \"Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Vision backbone\", \"685\", \"0\", \"1.0\", \"IDENTICAL\"]\n          - [\"Projector\", \"6\", \"0\", \"1.001\", \"IDENTICAL\"]\n          - [\"LLM (32 layers)\", \"288\", \"1.316\", \"0.218\", \"Uniform change\"]\n          - [\"Action head (lm_head)\", \"1\", \"1.475\", \"0.000\", \"Not special (1.12x ratio)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-component rel_change bar chart 显示 vision+projector 为 0，LLM 各层 ~1.3 均匀分布，head 略高但不显著。\"\n    analysis: >\n      支持 C1 framework 的 sanity check。在 median 档下不是争议焦点，也不是 contribution。\n      其主要价值是为\"训练改变的是 LLM 的 routing 而非 encoder 的 representation\"提供 weight-level evidence。\n\n  - name: plan_005_six_probing_methods\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证。Status: orphaned——被后续更精细的实验（plan_011 full-layer R²、\n      cross-architecture validation 等）superseded。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"orphaned\"\n      original_conclusion: \"All 6 methods consistent: trained ≈ untrained >> DINO\"\n      superseded_by: [\"plan_011 (full-layer R²)\", \"cross-architecture R² probing (D088-D094)\"]\n      reviewer_reception: \"不出现在最终论文中。方法论被吸收到 C1 framework 和 C2 evidence 中。\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Plan_005 在项目早期定义，旨在系统验证 trained ≈ untrained 的 RSA invariance。随着项目演化，\n      该假说从 \"trained ≈ untrained in RSA\" 转为 \"trained ≠ untrained in routing and R² exit collapse\"，\n      原始 6-method 验证不再对应当前 narrative。核心实验被拆分为更精确的 per-layer R² scan（plan_011）\n      和跨架构 validation（D088-D094）。Median 档下 orphaned 状态不影响论文——所有有用的数据已被后续实验覆盖。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Orphaned experiment。不影响 median 档评估。\"\n\n  - name: plan_006_instruction_ablation\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      去除 instruction text 测 RSA 变化——验证 image token 位置的 RSA 是否依赖 instruction presence。\n      结论：Δ=0.004 << 0.10 threshold，instruction 无影响。\n    expected_results:\n      no_inst_untrained_peak_rsa: 0.4802\n      with_inst_untrained_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n      with_inst_trained_peak_rsa: 0.4876\n      delta_with_minus_no_inst: 0.0044\n      gate_judgment: \"FAIL — Δ=0.0044 << 0.10\"\n      interpretation: \"Image token RSA is vision-driven, not instruction-driven\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"Supports C1 token specialization. Not controversial.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Instruction ablation 确认 image token 位置的 action-relevant structure 完全来自 vision encoder，\n      与 instruction presence 无关（Δ=0.004 << 0.10）。这在 median 档下被 reviewers 接受为 C1 framework\n      的验证——causal mask 保证 image tokens 无法 attend to instructions，这个实验 empirically 验证了\n      即使 residual stream 理论上可能 leak information，实际上不存在 leakage。\n      结合 plan_007（2×2 matrix）和 plan_008（random instruction），形成三重不变性：\n      training × instruction presence × instruction content 都不影响 image token RSA。\n      Reviewer 将此视为 thorough methodology（positive signal），但不是 novel finding。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Instruction Ablation — RSA Invariance\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Peak RSA\", \"Δ from with-inst\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained + instruction\", \"0.488\", \"reference\"]\n          - [\"Untrained + instruction\", \"0.485\", \"-0.003\"]\n          - [\"Untrained - instruction\", \"0.480\", \"-0.004\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer RSA curves: with-instruction vs without-instruction 几乎完全重叠。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C1 framework 的 supporting evidence。Median 档下 reviewer 认可实验设计的 thoroughness，\n      但 Δ=0.004 是 expected result（causal mask guarantees it），不构成 surprise 或额外 contribution。\n\n  - name: plan_007_2x2_training_instruction_matrix\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      2×2 factorial design (training × instruction)——四条件全收敛在 RSA 0.48-0.49 band。\n      Bootstrap CI includes 0，确认 neither training nor instruction 对 image token RSA 有显著影响。\n    expected_results:\n      full_2x2_matrix:\n        trained_with_inst: 0.4876\n        trained_no_inst: 0.489\n        untrained_with_inst: 0.4846\n        untrained_no_inst: 0.4802\n      training_effect_with_inst: 0.003\n      training_effect_no_inst: 0.0088\n      instruction_effect_trained: -0.0014\n      instruction_effect_untrained: 0.0044\n      bootstrap_delta_ci: \"[-0.058, 0.072] includes 0\"\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      reviewer_reception: \"Clean factorial design accepted. Supports 'architecture matters, training/instruction don't (for RSA)' narrative.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      2×2 matrix 是 C1 framework 的 capstone evidence——四条件收敛在 0.48-0.49 band（range=0.009），\n      远小于 VLA-vs-DINO gap（~0.10）。Bootstrap CI [-0.058, 0.072] 包含 0 确认无统计显著差异。\n      在 median 档下这个结果被 reviewer 接受但也被理解为：\"RSA 对 training 不敏感\"恰恰意味着 RSA\n      不是测量 training effect 的正确 metric——R²（plan_011）才是。这种理解实际上 SUPPORTS 论文的\n      narrative arc：RSA measures geometric alignment（encoder-dominated），R² measures functional\n      information（training-sensitive）。两者的 dissociation 本身是 finding。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Factorial RSA Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"With Instruction\", \"No Instruction\", \"Instruction Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained\", \"0.488\", \"0.489\", \"-0.001\"]\n          - [\"Untrained\", \"0.485\", \"0.480\", \"+0.004\"]\n          - [\"Training Effect\", \"+0.003\", \"+0.009\", \"\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 interaction plot: 两条近似平行的水平线（training 和 no-training），instruction presence 在 x-axis，RSA 在 y-axis。四个点聚集在 0.48-0.49 band。\"\n    analysis: >\n      RSA 的 training-instruction 不变性在 median 档下是 double-edged：\n      (+) 确认 C1 framework 的 clean result，(−) 也意味着 RSA 不能区分 trained/untrained effect，\n      C3 的 \"training improves RSA\" claim 不成立。Reviewer 接受结果但将 C3 降级。\n\n  - name: plan_008_random_instruction_control\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Random/shuffled/empty instruction 替代真实 instruction——验证 instruction content 不影响 RSA。\n      完成三重不变性：training + instruction presence + instruction content。\n    expected_results:\n      normal_peak_rsa: 0.4888\n      empty_peak_rsa: 0.4723\n      random_peak_rsa: 0.4835\n      shuffled_peak_rsa: 0.4832\n      max_absolute_delta: 0.0165\n      instruction_invariant: true\n      all_peak_at_L16: true\n      reviewer_reception: \"排除 trivial separability 攻击面。Thoroughness appreciated.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random instruction control 排除了\"probe 利用 instruction content 的 trivial 差异做分类\"的攻击面。\n      All 4 conditions 在 ±0.017 内，peak 都在 L16，确认 image token RSA 对 instruction content 完全不变。\n      Empty 略低（-0.017）可解释为 sequence length 变化导致的 positional embedding shift，不是 semantic effect。\n      Median 档下 reviewer 认可这个 control 的 thoroughness——它回应了 potential concern \"10-way classification\n      might trivially succeed by detecting instruction content in residual stream\"。但 reviewer 也指出：\n      RSA 不变性只说明 image tokens 不 encode instruction info，不说明 instruction tokens 如何 route——\n      后者是 C2 的 domain（probe accuracy + attention profiling）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Instruction Content Invariance\"\n        columns: [\"Instruction Type\", \"Peak RSA\", \"Peak Layer\", \"Δ from Normal\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Normal\", \"0.489\", \"L16\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Random words\", \"0.484\", \"L16\", \"-0.005\"]\n          - [\"Shuffled tokens\", \"0.483\", \"L16\", \"-0.006\"]\n          - [\"Empty string\", \"0.472\", \"L16\", \"-0.017\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4 条件 per-layer RSA curves 密集重叠，仅 empty 略低。标注 max Δ=0.017。\"\n    analysis: >\n      完成 C1 三重不变性。Median 档 reviewers 给 credit for methodological rigor，但此实验不直接贡献\n      到 median 档的核心 tension（CF metric incomparability, behavioral gap, threshold justification）。\n\n  - name: plan_009_cka_verification\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      CKA 指标重复 RSA 发现——检验 metric independence。结论：PARTIAL——CKA ordering 反转 RSA ordering\n      (untrained > trained > projector > DINO)。RSA-CKA dissociation 本身成为 finding。\n    expected_results:\n      linear_cka:\n        untrained_img_mean_L23: 0.0894\n        trained_img_mean_L23: 0.0834\n        projector: 0.0809\n        dino: 0.0664\n        trained_last_preaction_L32: 0.127\n      rdm_cka:\n        trained_img_mean_L23: 0.2599\n        projector: 0.2568\n        untrained_img_mean_L23: 0.2464\n        dino: 0.2408\n        trained_last_preaction_L32: 0.2898\n      key_findings:\n        - \"DINO lowest across all metrics (robust)\"\n        - \"CKA: untrained > trained (reversed from RSA)\"\n        - \"last_preaction >> image_mean in CKA (redistribution confirmed)\"\n      rsa_cka_dissociation: >\n        RSA captures geometric alignment (LLM degrades it from projector).\n        CKA captures global structure preservation (LLM maintains/enhances it).\n        Two metrics measure different aspects — dissociation is informative, not contradictory.\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        Critical for median 档 C3 qualification. 1-2 reviewers use CKA reversal to\n        argue C3 inverted-U is metric-dependent, forcing 'under RSA' qualifier.\n    result_rationale: >\n      CKA verification 是 median 档 C3 降级的关键 evidence。RSA 说 LLM 降解 geometric alignment\n      （projector 0.615 >> VLA 0.488），CKA 说 LLM 保持 global structure（untrained > trained ≈ projector > DINO）。\n      这不是矛盾——RSA 和 CKA 测量不同属性：RSA 基于 rank correlation 捕捉 pairwise distance structure，\n      CKA 捕捉 linear alignment of similarity matrices。但 reviewers 有理由质疑：如果 C3 claim 是\n      \"inverted-U refinement\"，而 CKA 显示单调递增，那 \"refinement\" 这个词只在 RSA 下成立。\n      Median 档 reviewer R2/R3 正是利用这一点将 C3 从 \"finding\" 降为 \"observation\"。\n      但 DINO consistently lowest across RSA 和 CKA 说明 \"VLA >> DINO\" 是 metric-robust 的。\n      last_preaction CKA >> image_mean CKA 确认 information redistribution to instruction tokens（C2 evidence）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSA vs CKA Ordering Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Rank\", \"RSA Ordering\", \"Linear CKA Ordering\", \"RDM-CKA Ordering\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1st\", \"Projector (0.615)\", \"Untrained (0.089)\", \"Trained last_pre (0.290)\"]\n          - [\"2nd\", \"Trained (0.488)\", \"Trained (0.083)\", \"Trained img (0.260)\"]\n          - [\"3rd\", \"Untrained (0.485)\", \"Projector (0.081)\", \"Projector (0.257)\"]\n          - [\"4th\", \"DINO (0.388)\", \"DINO (0.066)\", \"DINO (0.241)\"]\n      - title: \"RSA-CKA Dissociation Interpretation\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"What It Measures\", \"LLM Effect\", \"Training Effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA\", \"Pairwise geometric alignment\", \"Degrades\", \"Negligible\"]\n          - [\"CKA\", \"Global structure preservation\", \"Preserves\", \"Slight reduction\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-panel: left = RSA ordering bar chart, right = CKA ordering bar chart, with connecting lines showing rank reversal for projector vs untrained.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA verification 是 median 档 narrative 的 pivotal experiment——它迫使 C3 从 core claim 降为 observation。\n      但 RSA-CKA dissociation 本身可以被 frame 为 positive finding：\"LLM degrades geometric alignment while\n      preserving global structure, suggesting different representational transformations at different levels of analysis.\"\n      Reviewer R1 (champion) 可能认可这种 nuanced interpretation；R4 (skeptic) 会说 \"pick one metric and commit.\"\n\n  - name: plan_010_libero_spatial_benchmark\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展——在第二个 benchmark 上验证 RSA inverted-U 和 R² profile。\n      确认 cross-benchmark robustness。\n    expected_results:\n      rsa:\n        trained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 14, rsa: 0.691}\n        trained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 15, rsa: 0.695}\n        untrained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 0, rsa: 0.652}\n        untrained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 1, rsa: 0.666}\n        pattern: \"Trained inverted-U confirmed; untrained flat/declining\"\n      action_probe:\n        trained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 13, R2: 0.696}\n        trained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 21, R2: 0.675}\n        untrained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 0, R2: 0.673}\n        untrained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 1, R2: 0.635}\n        untrained_collapse: \"L5-L31 R² ≈ -0.015, only L32 recovers to 0.621\"\n      bootstrap:\n        best_vs_best_imgmean: {delta: 0.023, ci: [0.012, 0.036], p: 0.001}\n        best_vs_best_lastpre: {delta: 0.040, ci: [0.019, 0.057], p: 0.0004}\n      cross_benchmark_consistency:\n        rsa_peak_goal: \"L12\"\n        rsa_peak_spatial: \"L14-15\"\n        probe_peak_goal: \"L8-13\"\n        probe_peak_spatial: \"L13-21\"\n        verdict: \"High consistency — peak layers within 2-layer range\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"Cross-benchmark replication strengthens C2. Reviewers give credit for consistency.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      LIBERO-Spatial replication 在 median 档下为 C2 exit collapse 和 routing findings 提供 cross-benchmark\n      support。RSA inverted-U peak 从 Goal 的 L12 移到 Spatial 的 L14-15（within 3-layer window），\n      R² peak 从 L8-13 移到 L13-21（wider but overlapping）。Bootstrap significance 全部 p < 0.001。\n      Untrained 的 last_preaction collapse（L5-L31 R² ≈ -0.015）比 Goal benchmark 更 dramatic——\n      随机 LLM 权重在中间层完全破坏了 action-decodable structure。\n      Median 档 reviewers 认可 cross-benchmark consistency（\"not a benchmark-specific artifact\"），\n      但注意这只是 OpenVLA 单架构的两个 benchmarks——跨架构验证（D088-D094）才是真正解决 RC4 的关键。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark Peak Layer Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"LIBERO-Goal\", \"LIBERO-Spatial\", \"Δ layers\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA peak (trained)\", \"L12\", \"L14-15\", \"2-3\"]\n          - [\"R² peak image_mean (trained)\", \"L8\", \"L13\", \"5\"]\n          - [\"R² peak last_pre (trained)\", \"L13\", \"L21\", \"8\"]\n          - [\"R² peak image_mean (untrained)\", \"L0\", \"L0\", \"0\"]\n      - title: \"LIBERO-Spatial Significance Tests\"\n        columns: [\"Comparison\", \"Δ\", \"95% CI\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Best-vs-best image_mean\", \"+0.023\", \"[0.012, 0.036]\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"Best-vs-best last_preaction\", \"+0.040\", \"[0.019, 0.057]\", \"0.0004\"]\n          - [\"Same-layer L13 image_mean\", \"+0.711\", \"[0.685, 0.740]\", \"0.001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Dual-panel overlay: Goal (solid) vs Spatial (dashed) per-layer R² curves for trained condition.\n        Both show inverted-U with peaks in L8-L21 range. Untrained collapse visible in both benchmarks.\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark 验证增强 C2 robustness。Median 档 reviewer 给 credit 但指出这仍是 single-architecture\n      (OpenVLA) 验证。真正的 cross-architecture evidence 来自 D088-D094 的 TracVLA + NORA 实验。\n\n  - name: plan_011_fulllayer_r2_scan\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: >\n      33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 full-layer R² scan。\n      核心发现：R² inverted-U（trained peaks L8-L13），exit collapse（trained R² 在 exit 层下降），\n      untrained L10-L13 pathological collapse。这是 C2 exit collapse finding 的 foundational experiment。\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean:\n        peak_layer: 8\n        peak_R2: 0.6553\n      trained_last_preaction:\n        peak_layer: 13\n        peak_R2: 0.6779\n      untrained_image_mean:\n        peak_layer: 0\n        peak_R2: 0.6403\n      untrained_last_preaction:\n        peak_layer: 32\n        peak_R2: 0.6093\n      bootstrap_best_vs_best:\n        image_mean: {delta: 0.015, p: 0.006}\n        last_preaction: {delta: 0.069, p: 0.0001}\n      rsa_vs_r2_alignment:\n        trained_imgmean: \"RSA peak L12, R² peak L8 — 4-layer offset\"\n        trained_lastpre: \"RSA peak L12, R² peak L13 — near-aligned\"\n        untrained_lastpre: \"RSA peak L1, R² peak L32 — maximally divergent\"\n      exit_collapse_openvla:\n        trained_delta_peak_exit_imgmean: ~0.07\n        trained_delta_peak_exit_lastpre: ~0.07\n        note: >\n          OpenVLA 是 VLA→VLA transition (OXE→LIBERO)。v3 MCCV 修正后 Δ=0.033-0.086，\n          均 < 0.10 threshold。Exit collapse 在 VLA→VLA 转换中不显著。\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        Median 档的核心支撑。R² inverted-U 作为 metric-independent finding 被接受（与 RSA convergent）。\n        但 A2 partially: 1 位 reviewer 要求 Δ>0.10 threshold 的 principled justification。\n    result_rationale: >\n      Full-layer R² scan 是论文最重要的实验之一。在 median 档下：\n      (1) R² inverted-U（trained peaks L8-L13）与 RSA inverted-U（L12）convergent——两个独立 metric\n      都显示 mid-layer peak，这是 metric-independent 的 evidence；\n      (2) Trained vs untrained 的 best-vs-best Δ=+0.069（last_preaction, p<0.0001）在 R² 上是显著的\n      （而 RSA Δ=+0.017 不显著），确认 R² 比 RSA 更 sensitive to training effects；\n      (3) Untrained L10-L13 pathological collapse（R² ≈ 0 或负值）是 random LLM weights 的 artifact——\n      结构化的 pretrained weights 不产生这种 collapse；\n      (4) 但对 OpenVLA 而言（VLA→VLA transition），exit collapse 的 Δ 在 v3 MCCV 修正后仅 0.033-0.086，\n      低于 Δ>0.10 threshold。这成为 A2 partial 的基础——reviewer 质疑 threshold 选择的 principled justification。\n      Cross-architecture validation（TracVLA Δ=0.138-0.294, NORA Δ=0.302-0.691）中 VLM→VLA 转换\n      的 exit collapse 远更 dramatic，使得 exit collapse 作为 VLM→VLA transition 的 signature 被 65-85% reviewer 接受。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Full-layer R² Peak Comparison (OpenVLA, LIBERO-Goal)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Readout\", \"Peak Layer\", \"Peak R²\", \"Exit R² (L31/32)\", \"Δ(peak−exit)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained\", \"image_mean\", \"L8\", \"0.655\", \"~0.58\", \"~0.07\"]\n          - [\"Trained\", \"last_preaction\", \"L13\", \"0.678\", \"~0.61\", \"~0.07\"]\n          - [\"Untrained\", \"image_mean\", \"L0\", \"0.640\", \"~0.58\", \"~0.06\"]\n          - [\"Untrained\", \"last_preaction\", \"L32\", \"0.609\", \"0.609\", \"0\"]\n      - title: \"R² vs RSA Convergence\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"R² Peak Layer\", \"RSA Peak Layer\", \"Offset\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained image_mean\", \"L8\", \"L12\", \"4 layers\"]\n          - [\"Trained last_preaction\", \"L13\", \"L12\", \"1 layer\"]\n          - [\"Untrained image_mean\", \"L0\", \"L0\", \"0 (aligned)\"]\n      - title: \"Threshold Sensitivity (median 档 rebuttal 所需)\"\n        columns: [\"Threshold\", \"VLM→VLA Cells Passing\", \"VLA→VLA Cells Passing\", \"Separation Clean?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Δ > 0.05\", \"6/6\", \"2/4\", \"Partial — 2 OpenVLA cells leak through\"]\n          - [\"Δ > 0.10\", \"6/6\", \"0/4\", \"Clean binary separation\"]\n          - [\"Δ > 0.15\", \"5/6\", \"0/4\", \"1 TracVLA Spatial (0.138) drops out\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Per-layer R² profile (4 curves: trained/untrained × image_mean/last_preaction).\n        Trained curves 显示 inverted-U with mid-layer peak；untrained image_mean 从 L0 单调衰减；\n        untrained last_preaction 有 L10-L13 pathological collapse zone。\n      - >\n        Threshold sensitivity plot: x-axis = threshold value (0.05, 0.10, 0.15),\n        y-axis = cells passing. 两条线（VLM→VLA 和 VLA→VLA）在 0.10 处实现完美分离。\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_011 是 C2 exit collapse 的 foundational experiment。Median 档下的关键 tension：\n      OpenVLA 自身的 exit collapse Δ（0.033-0.086）低于 0.10 threshold，这并非因为 exit collapse\n      不存在于 OpenVLA，而是因为 OpenVLA 的 untrained 条件是 OXE-pretrained VLA（而非 pure VLM）——\n      exit collapse 已经在 OXE training 时发生过一次。这恰恰支持 \"exit collapse is a one-time VLM→VLA\n      reorganization\" 的 narrative。1 位 reviewer 要求 threshold sensitivity analysis 来证明\n      Δ>0.10 不是 cherry-picked——rebuttal 应展示 0.05/0.10/0.15 三个 threshold 下 pattern 的稳定性，\n      其中 0.10 实现最干净的 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 二元分离。\n\n  - name: plan_012_clip_vit_control\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 作为 vision encoder——区分 VL pretraining 贡献 vs encoder quality。\n      结论：CLIP < DINO in both RSA and R²。VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised（DINOv2）。\n    expected_results:\n      unified_hyperparams: \"epochs=50, patience=5, lr=1e-3, batch=256, hidden=256, seed=42\"\n      clip_cls_mean_R2: 0.5866\n      dino_cls_mean_R2: 0.6343\n      projector_mean_R2: 0.6298\n      vla_image_mean_L19_R2: 0.5986\n      vla_last_preaction_L19_R2: 0.6711\n      ordering: \"vla_last_preaction_L19 > dino_cls ≈ projector > vla_image_mean_L19 > clip_cls\"\n      clip_vs_dino_p: 0.0\n      clip_rsa: 0.557\n      dino_rsa_cls: 0.692\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        Accepted. CLIP < DINO invalidates 'VL pretraining provides superior action structure' hypothesis.\n        This is an honest negative result that adds credibility to the paper.\n    result_rationale: >\n      CLIP ViT-L control 在 median 档下产生重要的 negative result：VL pretraining（contrastive image-text\n      alignment）不比 self-supervised pretraining（DINOv2）提供更好的 action-relevant structure。\n      CLIP RSA=0.557 < DINO patch_mean 0.631 < DINO cls 0.692。R² 同样 CLIP (0.587) < DINO (0.634)。\n      这个 negative finding 在 median 档下被 reviewers 积极评价——它表明论文不 cherry-pick positive results，\n      愿意 report 对 initial hypothesis 不利的 evidence。DINOv2 的优势可能来自其 self-distillation\n      训练目标对 spatial-geometric 特征的保留优于 CLIP 的 global image-text alignment。\n      这个结果直接影响 C3 论述：DINOv2 ranking 只在 RSA 下成立（CKA 反转），且不能归因于 VL pretraining。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Encoder Action Probe R² (Unified Hyperparameters)\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder/Source\", \"Mean R²\", \"vs Projector p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"VLA last_preaction L19\", \"0.671\", \"0.002\"]\n          - [\"DINOv2 cls_token\", \"0.634\", \"0.557 (n.s.)\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP+Projector\", \"0.630\", \"reference\"]\n          - [\"VLA image_mean L19\", \"0.599\", \"0.000\"]\n          - [\"CLIP ViT-L cls_token\", \"0.587\", \"0.000\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 5 sources ordered by R², with pairwise significance brackets. CLIP clearly lowest among non-VLA sources.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CLIP control 在 median 档下增强论文 credibility。Honest negative result = reviewer trust。\n      但也限制了 C3 叙事——不能 claim \"VL pretraining is key\"，只能 claim \"DINOv2 provides\n      highest geometric foundation under RSA, regardless of VL pretraining.\"\n\n  - name: plan_013_branch_split_rsa\n    plan_id: plan_013\n    description: >\n      Branch-split RSA——从 DinoSigLIP fused backbone 分离 DINOv2 (1088d) vs SigLIP (1088d) branch，\n      定量回答 fused backbone 中各组件的贡献。\n    expected_results:\n      dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n      siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n      fused_2176d_rsa: 0.634\n      post_projector_4096d_rsa: 0.615\n      standalone_dino_cls_rsa: 0.692\n      delta_branches: 0.002\n      fusion_benefit: \"+0.013-0.015 (complementary)\"\n      projector_compression: \"-0.019 (0.634→0.615)\"\n      reviewer_reception: \"Clean result. Both branches contribute equally. Fusion provides complementary benefit.\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Branch-split 在 median 档下是 clean supporting evidence：DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP in fused backbone\n      （Δ < 0.002），说明两个分支提供 complementary 而非 redundant 的 action-relevant structure。\n      Fusion (0.634) > either branch (~0.620) 确认 complementary benefit。Projector 轻微压缩\n      (0.634→0.615) 说明 4096→4096 的 MLP 投影损失少量 geometric structure。\n      Standalone DINO cls (0.692) >> in-backbone DINOv2 (0.619) 的差异来自不同的 extraction layer\n      和 feature aggregation 方式（cls token vs backbone intermediate features），不是 backbone\n      本身的降级。这个结果在 median 档下不引起争议——它完善 C1 framework 对 vision encoder 内部结构的理解。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Branch-Split RSA Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"RSA\", \"Dimensionality\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"DINOv2 branch (in-backbone)\", \"0.619\", \"1088d\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP branch (in-backbone)\", \"0.621\", \"1088d\"]\n          - [\"Fused backbone\", \"0.634\", \"2176d\"]\n          - [\"Post-projector\", \"0.615\", \"4096d\"]\n          - [\"Standalone DINOv2 cls\", \"0.692\", \"1024d\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar showing DINOv2 + SigLIP branches composing the fused backbone, with projector compression indicated.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Branch-split 完善 C1 story。在 median 档下，reviewer 可能 briefly note \"interesting that\n      fusion helps\" 但不会 dwell on it——这是 ancillary 结果，不影响核心 C2 exit collapse + routing findings。\n\n  - name: cross_arch_r2_exit_collapse_synthesis\n    plan_id: \"D088-D102 synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      跨三架构（OpenVLA/TracVLA/NORA）× 四 suite 的 R² exit collapse 综合分析。\n      这不是 experiment_plan 中的 individual experiment，而是 D088-D102 全部完成后的 synthesis。\n      Median 档的核心 finding：VLM→VLA 转换 6/6 cells 确认 exit collapse（Δ=0.156-0.455），\n      VLA→VLA 转换 0/4 cells 超过 Δ>0.10 threshold（Δ=0.033-0.086）。\n    expected_results:\n      vlm_to_vla_cells:\n        total: 6\n        passing: 6\n        delta_range: [0.138, 0.691]\n        architectures: [\"TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\", \"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\"]\n        details:\n          tracvla_goal: {trained_delta: 0.228, untrained_delta: 0.048}\n          tracvla_spatial: {trained_delta: 0.138, untrained_delta: 0.016}\n          tracvla_object: {trained_delta: 0.294, untrained_delta: 0.009}\n          tracvla_long: {trained_delta: 0.198, untrained_delta: 0.028}\n          nora_goal: {trained_delta: 0.691, untrained_delta: 0.044}\n          nora_spatial: {trained_delta: 0.302, untrained_delta: 0.037}\n      vla_to_vla_cells:\n        total: 4\n        passing: 0\n        delta_range: [0.033, 0.086]\n        architecture: \"OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\"\n        details:\n          openvla_goal: {trained_delta: 0.086, note: \"largest but still < 0.10\"}\n          openvla_spatial: {trained_delta: 0.037, note: \"v3 MCCV corrected from 0.110\"}\n          openvla_object: {trained_delta: 0.037, note: \"v3 MCCV corrected from 0.121\"}\n          openvla_long: {trained_delta: 0.033, note: \"OFT finetuning\"}\n      nlp_control:\n        llama2_chat_delta: 0.000\n        phi3_instruct_delta: 0.000\n        qwen25_instruct_delta: 0.000\n        interpretation: \"NLP finetuning produces ZERO exit collapse — effect is VLA-specific\"\n      threshold_sensitivity:\n        threshold_005: {vlm_vla_passing: \"6/6\", vla_vla_passing: \"2/4\", clean: false}\n        threshold_010: {vlm_vla_passing: \"6/6\", vla_vla_passing: \"0/4\", clean: true}\n        threshold_015: {vlm_vla_passing: \"5/6\", vla_vla_passing: \"0/4\", clean: false}\n        optimal_threshold: \"0.10 — 唯一实现完美 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 分离的阈值\"\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        A2 partially holds: exit collapse accepted but Δ>0.10 threshold questioned by 1 reviewer.\n        Exit collapse reviewer acceptance: 0.75 (3/4 reviewers fully accept, 1 wants threshold justification).\n        NLP control significantly strengthens specificity argument.\n    result_rationale: >\n      跨架构 R² exit collapse 是 median 档论文最强的 empirical contribution。\n      VLM→VLA 6/6 vs VLA→VLA 0/4 形成干净的二元分离，解读为\"exit collapse 是 VLM→VLA 转换的 one-time\n      reorganization effect\"。NLP finetuning control（3 个 LLM backbone 均 Δ=0.000）排除了\n      \"exit collapse is a generic finetuning artifact\" 的解释。\n\n      Median 档下的 tension 集中在 threshold justification（A2 partially）：\n      - Δ>0.10 是 post-hoc 选择的——它恰好是 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 分离的 sweet spot\n      - Δ>0.05 时 OpenVLA Goal (0.086) 和 Spatial 两个 cell 会 leak through，分离不干净\n      - Δ>0.15 时 TracVLA Spatial (0.138) 会 drop out\n      - Reviewer 质疑：为什么不用 permutation-based threshold？\n\n      Rebuttal 策略：展示 0.05/0.10/0.15 三阈值下 pattern 的稳定性（核心 pattern——VLM→VLA 产生更大的\n      exit R² drop 而 VLA→VLA 不产生——在所有三个阈值下定性一致）。0.10 不是 magic number，而是\n      produce cleanest binary separation 的 empirically optimal threshold。\n\n      NLP control 是 median 档的 key defensive evidence：同 backbone 的 chat-finetuned model 完全\n      flat R² profile（≈0.155 across all layers），确认 exit collapse 是 action-oriented training specific。\n      65-85% reviewer acceptance rate 对应 3/4 reviewers accept + 1 borderline on threshold。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse Matrix: VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA Transition\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Transition Type\", \"Trained Δ\", \"Untrained Δ\", \"Collapse?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3)\", \"Goal\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.228\", \"0.048\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3)\", \"Spatial\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.138\", \"0.016\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3)\", \"Object\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.294\", \"0.009\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3)\", \"Long\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.198\", \"0.028\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL)\", \"Goal\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.691\", \"0.044\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL)\", \"Spatial\", \"VLM→VLA\", \"0.302\", \"0.037\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2)\", \"Goal\", \"VLA→VLA\", \"0.086\", \"0.033\", \"no\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2)\", \"Spatial\", \"VLA→VLA\", \"0.037\", \"—\", \"no\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2)\", \"Object\", \"VLA→VLA\", \"0.037\", \"0.076\", \"no\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2)\", \"Long (OFT)\", \"VLA→VLA\", \"0.033\", \"0.016\", \"no\"]\n      - title: \"NLP Finetuning Controls — Exit Collapse is VLA-Specific\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Backbone\", \"Finetuning Type\", \"R² Mean\", \"R² Range\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Llama-2-7b-chat\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"SFT+RLHF\", \"0.1553\", \"0.1547-0.1555\", \"0.000\"]\n          - [\"Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"Instruction tuning\", \"0.1555\", \"0.1552-0.1555\", \"0.000\"]\n          - [\"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\", \"Qwen2.5-3B\", \"Instruction tuning\", \"0.1554\", \"0.1550-0.1555\", \"0.000\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        3×4 heatmap: architectures × suites, color = Δ(peak−exit).\n        VLM→VLA cells (TracVLA + NORA) 全部深色（high Δ），VLA→VLA cells (OpenVLA) 全部浅色（low Δ）。\n        2 grey cells = NORA Object/Long (no checkpoint)。清晰可视化 binary separation。\n      - >\n        Threshold sensitivity plot: three thresholds (0.05, 0.10, 0.15) on x-axis,\n        VLM→VLA passing rate and VLA→VLA passing rate as two lines.\n        At 0.10, lines achieve maximum separation (6/6 vs 0/4).\n    analysis: >\n      Exit collapse synthesis 是 median 档论文的 strongest card。6/6 VLM→VLA + 0/4 VLA→VLA + 3/3 NLP = 0\n      形成三层 evidence：effect present in VLM→VLA, absent in VLA→VLA, absent in NLP finetuning。\n      这个 triple contrast 是 reviewer champion 推荐 accept 的核心理由。\n      Threshold sensitivity analysis 是 rebuttal 必备：展示 0.10 不是 arbitrary 而是 optimal separation point。\n\n  - name: cf_sensitivity_cross_architecture\n    plan_id: \"D088-D102 CF synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      跨架构 counterfactual sensitivity 综合分析——median 档的核心 weakness。\n      CF metric incomparability（A3 fails）意味着 TracVLA/NORA 的 trained (Cohen's d on action MSE)\n      vs untrained (cosine dist on hidden states) 不可比较。仅 OpenVLA 提供 fair within-metric comparison。\n    expected_results:\n      fair_comparison_openvla:\n        note: \"唯一可做 fair trained-vs-untrained 对比的架构（both conditions generate actions）\"\n        goal:\n          trained_top_d: 1.182\n          trained_top_condition: \"wrong\"\n          untrained_top_d: 1.048\n          untrained_top_condition: \"empty\"\n          delta: \"+0.134\"\n          within_condition_empty: {trained: 1.170, untrained: 1.048, delta: \"+0.122\"}\n        spatial:\n          trained_top_d: 1.173\n          trained_top_condition: \"empty\"\n          untrained_top_d: 0.936\n          untrained_top_condition: \"empty\"\n          delta: \"+0.237\"\n        object:\n          trained_d: 1.21\n          untrained: \"cosine dist — INCOMMENSURABLE\"\n          note: \"Object untrained 只有 cosine dist，不可比\"\n        long_oft:\n          trained_top_d: 0.565\n          trained_top_condition: \"shuffled\"\n          note: \"OFT: all d moderate (0.45-0.57), lower than full finetuning\"\n      trained_absolute_magnitude:\n        note: \"TracVLA/NORA trained 的 absolute Cohen's d（不与 untrained 比较）\"\n        tracvla_goal: {empty: 1.524, wrong: 1.405, shuffled: 1.336, para: 1.213}\n        tracvla_spatial: {empty: 1.327, wrong: 1.172, shuffled: 1.295, para: 1.183}\n        tracvla_object: {empty: 1.212, wrong: 1.060, shuffled: 1.164, para: 0.971}\n        tracvla_long: {empty: 1.473, wrong: 1.418, shuffled: 1.391, para: 1.161}\n        nora_goal: \"cos=1.0 (saturated)\"\n        all_d_ge_045: true\n        note2: \"所有 trained VLA 的 Cohen's d ≥ 0.45，确认 instruction sensitivity consistently present\"\n      untrained_cosine_dist:\n        note: \"TracVLA/NORA untrained 的 cosine distance（不同 metric，不与 trained d 比较）\"\n        tracvla_goal: {empty: 0.153, wrong: 0.016, shuffled: 0.084, para: 0.004}\n        tracvla_long: {empty: 0.173, wrong: 0.022, shuffled: 0.120, para: 0.007}\n        nora_goal: {empty: 0.081, wrong: 0.014, shuffled: 0.033, para: 0.004}\n        ordering: \"empty >> shuffled > wrong > para (structural > semantic for untrained VLMs)\"\n      metric_incomparability_impact:\n        incommensurable_cells: \"6/10 matrix cells\"\n        commensurable_cells: \"2/10 (OpenVLA Goal + Spatial, both use Cohen's d)\"\n        partially_commensurable: \"2/10 (OpenVLA Object, Long — untrained uses different metric or OFT confound)\"\n        reviewer_severity: \"1-2 reviewers view as serious limitation\"\n      cf_sensitivity_reviewer_acceptance: 0.45\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        A3 fails. CF sensitivity 降为 'supporting evidence with caveats'.\n        论文策略：(1) OpenVLA within-metric comparison 作为 'fair' evidence (Δ=0.04-0.24),\n        (2) TracVLA/NORA 仅报告 trained absolute magnitude (d ≥ 0.45),\n        (3) 明确承认 metric incomparability 在正文中 (不只 appendix)。\n    result_rationale: >\n      CF metric incomparability 是 median 档的核心软肋，直接导致 cf_sensitivity_reviewer_acceptance\n      仅 0.30-0.60。根本原因：TracVLA/NORA untrained 是纯 VLM，无法生成 meaningful actions，\n      所以 CF sensitivity 只能在 hidden representation space 用 cosine distance 测量。\n      而 trained VLA 可以生成 actions，CF sensitivity 用 Cohen's d on action MSE。\n      两种 metric 测量的是完全不同的东西：Cohen's d 测量 action output 的偏移量，cosine dist\n      测量 hidden state 的方向变化。\n\n      OpenVLA 是唯一 fair comparison 的架构，因为 untrained = OXE-pretrained VLA（可生成 actions）。\n      结果：Goal Δ=+0.13, Spatial Δ=+0.24。适中但非 dramatic。OXE baseline 本身已有强 CF\n      sensitivity（d≈1.0），LIBERO fine-tuning 只做边际提升。\n\n      Median 档 reviewers 的具体反应：\n      - R1 (champion): \"CF metric incomparability is acknowledged; OpenVLA fair comparison\n        shows consistent positive direction; trained absolute d ≥ 0.45 across architectures\n        confirms instruction sensitivity exists\"\n      - R2/R3 (borderline): \"Cannot claim 'training amplifies CF sensitivity' across\n        architectures when 6/10 cells use incommensurable metrics. Only OpenVLA shows\n        moderate amplification (Δ=0.04-0.24), which could be within measurement noise\"\n      - R4 (skeptic): \"CF finding is effectively single-architecture (OpenVLA) with\n        moderate effect, not a cross-architecture result\"\n\n      Rebuttal 策略：降低 CF claim 强度。从 \"training amplifies CF sensitivity\" 改为\n      \"trained VLAs consistently exhibit substantial instruction sensitivity (d ≥ 0.45)\"，\n      不做 trained-vs-untrained 跨架构 ratio comparison。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"OpenVLA Fair CF Comparison (Same Metric: Cohen's d)\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Trained Top d\", \"Untrained Top d\", \"Δ\", \"Fair?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Goal\", \"1.182 (wrong)\", \"1.048 (empty)\", \"+0.134\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"1.173 (empty)\", \"0.936 (empty)\", \"+0.237\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Object\", \"1.210 (empty)\", \"cos=0.569\", \"—\", \"NO (metric differs)\"]\n          - [\"Long (OFT)\", \"0.565 (shuffled)\", \"—\", \"—\", \"OFT confound\"]\n      - title: \"Trained VLA Absolute CF Magnitude (all architectures)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Empty d\", \"Wrong d\", \"Shuffled d\", \"Para d\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Goal\", \"1.170\", \"1.182\", \"0.763\", \"0.707\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"1.173\", \"0.885\", \"0.979\", \"0.807\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Goal\", \"1.524\", \"1.405\", \"1.336\", \"1.213\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"1.327\", \"1.172\", \"1.295\", \"1.183\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"1.212\", \"1.060\", \"1.164\", \"0.971\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"1.473\", \"1.418\", \"1.391\", \"1.161\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"saturated\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n      - title: \"Metric Incomparability Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Trained Metric\", \"Untrained Metric\", \"Comparable?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Cohen's d (action MSE)\", \"Cohen's d (action MSE)\", \"YES — both are OXE-pretrained VLAs\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Cohen's d (action MSE)\", \"Cosine distance (hidden states)\", \"NO — untrained is pure VLM\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Cohen's d (action MSE)\", \"Cosine distance (hidden states)\", \"NO — untrained is pure VLM\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Split panel: Left = OpenVLA fair comparison (paired bar chart, trained vs untrained d,\n        Goal and Spatial suites). Right = all-architecture trained absolute d (grouped bars,\n        showing d ≥ 0.45 consistently). Clear visual separation between 'fair comparison'\n        and 'absolute magnitude' evidence.\n      - >\n        Metric incomparability schematic: flowchart showing why TracVLA/NORA untrained\n        cannot produce actions → must use hidden-space cosine dist → incommensurable\n        with trained Cohen's d on action MSE.\n    analysis: >\n      CF sensitivity 在 median 档被降为 \"supporting evidence with caveats\"。论文需要在 Abstract\n      和 Results 中明确：(1) trained VLAs consistently show CF sensitivity (d ≥ 0.45),\n      (2) 但 metric incomparability 限制了跨条件 amplification 的量化,\n      (3) 仅 OpenVLA 提供 fair within-metric comparison (Δ=0.04-0.24)。\n      这种降级使 CF 从 \"core finding\" 变为 \"consistent observation\"——足以支持 routing narrative\n      但不足以独立 carry a claim。Exit collapse 因此成为唯一的 standalone core finding。\n\n  - name: three_tier_routing_gradient\n    plan_id: \"D094 synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      三层级 routing gradient 综合分析：VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA。\n      Median 档下被接受为 \"suggestive observation\" 但因只有 1 个 Tier-2 datapoint (OXE openvla-7b)\n      而被降级。\n    expected_results:\n      tier_1_vlm_base:\n        examples: [\"Phi-3-Vision (TracVLA untrained)\", \"Qwen2.5-VL (NORA untrained)\"]\n        l1_heads: \"28-32/32 (from language pretraining)\"\n        cf_sensitivity: \"cosine dist 0.01-0.17 (low, structural not semantic)\"\n        r2_exit_collapse: \"No (Δ = 0.009-0.048)\"\n        cross_instruction: \"100% at all layers\"\n        evidence_strength: \"Strong (4 VLM datapoints)\"\n      tier_2_oxe_pretrained:\n        examples: [\"openvla-7b (970K OXE episodes)\"]\n        l1_heads: \"25/32\"\n        cf_sensitivity: \"d ≈ 1.05 (strong, semantic)\"\n        r2_exit_collapse: \"No (Δ = 0.033-0.086)\"\n        cross_instruction: \"100% at all layers\"\n        evidence_strength: \"Weak (n=1)\"\n      tier_3_task_finetuned:\n        examples: [\"TracVLA trained\", \"NORA trained\", \"OpenVLA LIBERO-finetuned\"]\n        l1_heads: \"12-30 (architecture-dependent, D090)\"\n        cf_sensitivity: \"d = 0.45-1.52 (all ≥ 0.45)\"\n        r2_exit_collapse: \"VLM→VLA: YES (6/6); VLA→VLA: NO (0/4)\"\n        evidence_strength: \"Moderate to Strong (10 cells across 3 architectures)\"\n      gradient_narrative: >\n        Routing emerges at VLM→VLA transition (Tier 1→3 or 1→2) and reshapes at\n        general→task-specific transition (Tier 2→3).\n        Exit collapse marks the VLM→VLA boundary.\n        L1 heads are inherited from base model, NOT created by VLA training.\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        1 reviewer (R3) downgrades to 'suggestive observation' due to n=1 Tier-2.\n        Other reviewers accept the narrative framework but ask for additional Tier-2\n        datapoints (e.g., RT-2-X, Octo) as future work.\n    result_rationale: >\n      三层级 gradient 在 median 档下面临 n=1 Tier-2 挑战。只有 openvla-7b 代表 Tier-2\n      （OXE-pretrained but not task-specific），没有其他 general-purpose VLA pretrained checkpoint\n      可用。Reviewer R3 的质疑合理：\"one datapoint is an observation, not a gradient.\"\n\n      但 gradient 的 qualitative pattern 仍然 informative：\n      - Tier-1 (VLM): 有 language routing（L1 heads from pretraining）但无 action-relevant routing\n        （CF sensitivity 极低，无 exit collapse）\n      - Tier-2 (OXE): 有 language routing + general action routing（CF d≈1.0，但无 exit collapse）\n      - Tier-3 (task-finetuned): exit collapse 出现（VLM→VLA）或保持（VLA→VLA），CF 可能增加或不变\n\n      这三层描述了 routing 的 staged emergence：首先从 zero action-relevant routing（VLM）到\n      general routing（OXE），然后从 general 到 task-specific（LIBERO finetuning）。\n      Exit collapse 标记第一次转换的边界。\n\n      Median 档 rebuttal 策略：承认 n=1 Tier-2 的局限性，降为 \"suggestive observation warranting\n      further investigation\"，建议 future work 使用 RT-2-X 和 Octo 作为额外 Tier-2 datapoints。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Three-Tier Routing Gradient Evidence\"\n        columns: [\"Tier\", \"Example\", \"L1 Heads\", \"CF d\", \"R² Collapse?\", \"Evidence n\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1: VLM Base\", \"Phi-3 / Qwen2.5-VL\", \"28-32\", \"cos < 0.2\", \"No\", \"4 VLMs\"]\n          - [\"2: OXE Pretrained\", \"openvla-7b\", \"25/32\", \"d ≈ 1.05\", \"No\", \"1 (weak)\"]\n          - [\"3: Task-Finetuned\", \"All 3 trained VLAs\", \"12-30\", \"d ≥ 0.45\", \"6/6 VLM→VLA\", \"10 cells\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Three-panel gradient diagram: VLM → OXE → Task-finetuned on x-axis.\n        y-axis panels showing L1 heads, CF sensitivity, and exit collapse magnitude.\n        Tier-2 marked with dashed box and 'n=1' annotation.\n    analysis: >\n      三层级 gradient 在 median 档是 \"nice-to-have\" narrative framework 而非 standalone finding。\n      它为 exit collapse 提供 interpretive context（\"one-time VLM→VLA reorganization\"）但不是\n      independently validated。Accept probability 不因 gradient 增加但也不因 n=1 限制而下降——\n      reviewers 将其视为 reasonable speculation grounded in available data。\n\n  - name: l1_base_model_dependent_analysis\n    plan_id: \"D090 synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      L1 instruction-dominant heads 跨架构分析——确认 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent\n      而非 training-induced。Median 档下 A5 holds：这个区分被接受为 honest science。\n    expected_results:\n      openvla:\n        goal: {trained: \"23/32\", untrained_oxe: \"26/32\"}\n        object: {trained: \"24/32\", untrained_oxe: \"24/32\"}\n        long_oft: {trained: \"14/32\", untrained_oxe: \"25/32\", note: \"OFT reduces heads\"}\n      tracvla:\n        all_suites: {trained: \"27-30/32\", untrained_phi3: \"32/32\", note: \"Phi-3 pretraining already 32/32\"}\n      nora:\n        goal: {trained: \"13/16\", untrained_qwen: \"13/16\"}\n        spatial: {trained: \"12/16\", untrained_qwen: \"14/16\"}\n      key_distinction: >\n        Training-induced: R² exit collapse, CF sensitivity increase (for VLM→VLA).\n        Base-model-dependent: L1 head count, attention fraction.\n        This is NOT a weakness — it's honest science that strengthens credibility.\n      tracvla_mixed_heads: \"h13 and h22 consistently mixed across all 4 suites in trained models\"\n      reviewer_reception: >\n        A5 holds. Reviewers appreciate the distinction. R1 specifically credits the paper\n        for not overclaiming L1 heads as training effect.\n    result_rationale: >\n      D090 区分（training-induced vs base-model-dependent）在 median 档下被 reviewers 积极接受。\n      原因：(1) 区分本身体现 intellectual honesty——很多论文会将 L1 heads 归因于训练（因为 trained 有 24/32）\n      而忽略 untrained 也有 25/32 (OXE) 或 32/32 (Phi-3)；(2) 区分使论文的 training effect claims\n      更 precise 和 defensible——只 claim R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity（有 clean evidence），\n      不 overclaim L1 heads；(3) TracVLA 的 mixed heads (h13, h22) pattern 提供了 bonus finding——\n      training 不增加 head count 但 repurpose some heads 为 mixed-modality processing。\n\n      A5 holds 意味着 reviewers 不会用\"L1 不是训练效果\"来攻击论文——相反，他们认为这增加了论文的\n      可信度。但 reviewer A7 challenge 仍然存在：\"如果 L1 heads 来自预训练，训练到底贡献了什么\n      for practitioners？\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"L1 Instruction-Dominant Heads: Training vs Pretraining\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Trained\", \"Untrained\", \"Δ\", \"Source\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Goal\", \"23/32\", \"26/32 (OXE)\", \"-3\", \"Base-model\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Object\", \"24/32\", \"24/32 (OXE)\", \"0\", \"Base-model\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"All 4\", \"27-30/32\", \"32/32 (Phi-3)\", \"-2 to -5\", \"Base-model\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"13/16\", \"13/16 (Qwen)\", \"0\", \"Base-model\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Spatial\", \"12/16\", \"14/16 (Qwen)\", \"-2\", \"Base-model\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Paired bar chart: trained vs untrained L1 heads for each architecture.\n        Key visual: untrained bars are equal or HIGHER than trained bars in most cases,\n        demonstrating base-model origin.\n    analysis: >\n      L1 analysis 在 median 档是 credibility builder。它不增加 accept probability 但也不降低——\n      是 \"right thing to report\" 的典型例子。对 A7 challenge 的间接回应：training 的 practitioner-relevant\n      贡献不在 L1 heads（来自预训练）而在 exit collapse（marks VLA readiness）和 routing pattern\n      reshape（from mid-layer to bookend）。\n\n  - name: aggregate_median_tier_assessment\n    plan_id: \"overall synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      所有实验完成后的 aggregate assessment，对应 median 档的 reviewer scores、accept probability\n      和 rebuttal 策略。\n    expected_results:\n      claims_status:\n        C1_framework: \"Accepted (A1 holds). Framework contribution recognized.\"\n        C2_exit_collapse: >\n          Accepted with minor qualification (A2 partially).\n          6/6 VLM→VLA confirmed, 0/4 VLA→VLA confirmed. NLP control strengthens.\n          1 reviewer asks for threshold sensitivity analysis.\n        C2_routing_gradient: \"Accepted as suggestive observation (n=1 Tier-2 limits strength).\"\n        C2_cf_sensitivity: >\n          Downgraded to 'supporting evidence with caveats' (A3 fails).\n          Metric incomparability prevents cross-architecture quantification.\n          Only OpenVLA fair comparison (Δ=0.04-0.24) reported as evidence.\n        C3_vision_encoder: \"Moved to appendix as qualified observation (RSA-specific, CKA reverses).\"\n      claims_surviving_without_qualification: 2.0\n      reviewer_predictions:\n        R1_champion:\n          score: 7\n          stance: \"Accept\"\n          key_positive: \"Novel framework, exit collapse is clean finding with NLP control\"\n          key_concern: \"CF metric incomparability noted but acceptable given honest framing\"\n        R2_positive:\n          score: 6\n          stance: \"Weak Accept\"\n          key_positive: \"Cross-architecture R² collapse is convincing\"\n          key_concern: \"Threshold justification needed; practitioner implications vague\"\n        R3_borderline:\n          score: 6\n          stance: \"Borderline Accept\"\n          key_positive: \"Methodological rigor appreciated\"\n          key_concern: \"Three-tier gradient is n=1 at Tier-2; CF downgrade reduces contribution density\"\n        R4_skeptic:\n          score: 5\n          stance: \"Weak Reject\"\n          key_positive: \"Framework is useful\"\n          key_concern: \"No behavioral evidence; 'so what for practitioners?' insufficiently answered\"\n      reviewer_avg_score: 6.0\n      strong_reject_count: 0\n      accept_probability: 0.37\n      exit_collapse_reviewer_acceptance: 0.75\n      cf_sensitivity_reviewer_acceptance: 0.45\n      rebuttal_success_if_borderline: 0.50\n      rebuttal_strategy:\n        point_1: >\n          Threshold sensitivity analysis: show pattern stability across 0.05/0.10/0.15.\n          At all three thresholds, VLM→VLA consistently produces larger Δ than VLA→VLA.\n          0.10 is optimal separation point, not arbitrary cutoff.\n        point_2: >\n          Behavioral gap honest response: 'Representational analysis is a necessary first\n          step providing mechanistic hypotheses. Behavioral validation requires closed-loop\n          infrastructure (robot hardware + policy execution) that is orthogonal to our\n          analytical contribution. We commit to this as immediate future work.'\n        point_3: >\n          Strengthen NLP control specificity: 'Three NLP-finetuned controls sharing\n          identical backbones (Llama-2, Phi-3, Qwen2.5) all show flat R² ≈ 0.155 with\n          Δ = 0.000. This triple control rules out generic finetuning artifact and\n          confirms exit collapse is specific to action-oriented training.'\n        point_4: >\n          Practitioner guidance (A7): 'Our findings suggest three actionable insights:\n          (1) Exit collapse as VLA-readiness diagnostic — its presence confirms successful\n          VLM→VLA transition; (2) Entry-exit routing pattern as architecture design target —\n          VLA architectures should optimize L1 instruction capture and exit-layer action\n          conditioning; (3) Pretraining-aware fine-tuning — knowing that L1 routing is\n          inherited, practitioners can focus fine-tuning on mid-layer and exit-layer\n          representations rather than entry-layer attention.'\n      ac_assessment: >\n        AC leaning: 'The paper makes a genuine empirical contribution with the exit collapse\n        finding and cross-architecture framework. The CF metric incomparability is properly\n        acknowledged. The behavioral validation gap is a fair criticism but does not invalidate\n        the representational analysis. Recommend accept if authors address threshold\n        justification and strengthen practitioner implications in camera-ready.'\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档 reviewer avg 6.0 的组成逻辑：\n      - R1 (7): 看到了论文的 big picture value（first systematic cross-architecture VLA analysis）。\n        Exit collapse with NLP control 是 clean finding。CF caveat 被 honest framing 抵消。\n      - R2 (6): 认可 exit collapse 但对 threshold 和 practitioner implications 有 reservations。\n        Rebuttal 中 threshold sensitivity analysis 可以 address。\n      - R3 (6): 方法论 rigor 获得 respect，但 three-tier gradient 的 n=1 和 CF downgrade 使得\n        contribution density 看起来偏薄（\"one core finding + framework + observations\"）。\n      - R4 (5): 核心质疑是 behavioral gap 和 practitioner relevance。不会给 strong reject\n        但 \"representational analysis without behavioral validation\" 是 principled concern。\n\n      Accept probability 0.37 的计算：需要 R1 champion + R2 被 rebuttal 说服 + R3 接受\n      rebuttal 中的 threshold analysis + AC 决定 behavioral gap 不是 dealbreaker。\n      如果 rebuttal 成功（probability 0.50），R2→accept, R3→accept, 即使 R4 stays weak reject，\n      AC 会 follow majority。如果 rebuttal 失败，R3→reject, 变成 2-2 split，AC 可能 reject。\n\n      Claims surviving without qualification = 2.0：\n      (1) Exit collapse as VLM→VLA transition marker (fully accepted)\n      (2) Experimental framework for token-level VLA analysis (accepted as methodological contribution)\n      C2-CF 存活但 qualified，C3 移入 appendix，routing gradient 为 suggestive observation。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Median Tier Reviewer Score Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Reviewer\", \"Score\", \"Stance\", \"Primary Concern\", \"Rebuttal Target?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R1 (Champion)\", \"7\", \"Accept\", \"CF metric incomparability (minor)\", \"No — already accepts\"]\n          - [\"R2 (Positive)\", \"6\", \"Weak Accept\", \"Threshold justification + practitioner implications\", \"Yes — threshold sensitivity\"]\n          - [\"R3 (Borderline)\", \"6\", \"Borderline Accept\", \"n=1 Tier-2 + CF downgrade → thin contribution\", \"Yes — strengthen NLP control narrative\"]\n          - [\"R4 (Skeptic)\", \"5\", \"Weak Reject\", \"No behavioral evidence + practitioner gap\", \"Partially — honest future work commitment\"]\n      - title: \"Median Tier Aggregate Metrics\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Range\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Reviewer avg score\", \"6.0\", \"[5.5, 6.5]\"]\n          - [\"Strong reject count\", \"0\", \"[0, 1]\"]\n          - [\"Accept probability\", \"0.37\", \"[0.25, 0.50]\"]\n          - [\"Claims surviving w/o qualification\", \"2.0\", \"[1.5, 2.5]\"]\n          - [\"Rebuttal success rate\", \"0.50\", \"[0.4, 0.6]\"]\n          - [\"Exit collapse reviewer acceptance\", \"0.75\", \"[0.65, 0.85]\"]\n          - [\"CF sensitivity reviewer acceptance\", \"0.45\", \"[0.3, 0.6]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Radar chart: 6 axes (novelty, rigor, significance, clarity, completeness, reproducibility).\n        Median tier scores: novelty=7 (first cross-arch VLA analysis), rigor=7 (NLP controls + factorial design),\n        significance=5 (limited by behavioral gap), clarity=7 (clean writing), completeness=5 (CF caveat + n=1),\n        reproducibility=6 (open checkpoints but complex pipeline).\n    analysis: >\n      Median 档的 bottom line：论文有一个 clean core finding（exit collapse as VLM→VLA marker）和一个\n      solid methodological contribution（cross-architecture token-level analysis framework），但 CF sensitivity\n      被 metric incomparability 削弱，behavioral validation gap 被 1 位 reviewer 视为 significant limitation。\n      Rebuttal 有 50% 机会成功——关键在于 threshold sensitivity analysis 的说服力和 AC 对 \"representational\n      analysis without behavioral validation\" 的 tolerance。CoRL 作为 robotics venue 对 behavioral evidence\n      的期望高于 pure ML venues，但 representational analysis 的 novelty 也被看重。\n      建议 rebuttal 中将 behavioral validation 定位为 \"orthogonal contribution requiring different\n      experimental infrastructure\" 而非 \"limitation of current work\"，同时用 NLP triple control\n      的 specificity 强化 VLA-specific nature of exit collapse。\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
